"locale":"en"},"7287":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-269","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#events","content":"`runtime`: the torch version, the loaded models and the engines' state (as `GET /runtime`)","locale":"en"},"7288":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-270","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#events","content":"`compute_changed`","locale":"en"},"7289":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-271","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#events","content":"`usage`: devices and memory","locale":"en"},"7290":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-272","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#events","content":"`settings_changed`","locale":"en"},"7291":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-273","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#events","content":"`keys`: the settings that changed","locale":"en"},"7292":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-274","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"Hear the audio as it is made. The protocol:","locale":"en"},"7293":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-275","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"The client sends one JSON text message: a `SpeakRequest`.","locale":"en"},"7294":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-276","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"The server answers `{\"type\": \"queued\", \"job_id\": …}`.","locale":"en"},"7295":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-277","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"When generation starts: `{\"type\": \"start\", \"job_id\": …, \"sample_rate\": 24000, \"granularity\": \"token\" | \"segment\" | \"emulated\"}`.","locale":"en"},"7296":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-278","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"Then binary messages: mono 16-bit little-endian PCM at the `start` rate, with `{\"type\": \"segment\", \"index\": n}` before each segment.","locale":"en"},"7297":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-279","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"Finally `{\"type\": \"end\", \"job_id\": …, \"output_ids\": […], \"output_id\": …}` or `{\"type\": \"error\", \"code\", \"message\", \"detail\"}`.","locale":"en"},"7298":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-280","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"A binary message is always audio; everything else is JSON text. The whole audio is still stored as a result (`output_id`). The client may send `{\"type\": \"cancel\"}` at any time.","locale":"en"},"7299":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-281","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"`granularity` says how fine the audio arrives: `token` as the model emits tokens (CosyVoice), `segment` once per segment, `emulated` when the model does not stream and Mizuoto splits the text to emulate it.","locale":"en"},"7300":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-282","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"**Streaming text**: with a model that has **Streaming text** (CosyVoice 2 and 3), set `\"text_stream\": true`; `text` is only the beginning. Send the rest as `{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"…\"}` messages and `{\"type\": \"flush\"}` after the last. Leaving before the flush cancels the job.","locale":"en"},"7301":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-283","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"Where a WebSocket is awkward, add `stream=true` to the same request: the response is the audio as it is made (chunked transfer):","locale":"en"},"7302":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-284","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"7303":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-285","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"Response","locale":"en"},"7304":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-286","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"`stream_format=wav` (default)","locale":"en"},"7305":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-287","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"A WAV of unknown length (PCM16 right after the header)","locale":"en"},"7306":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-288","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"`stream_format=pcm`","locale":"en"},"7307":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-289","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"Mono 16-bit little-endian PCM, no header","locale":"en"},"7308":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-290","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"The `X-Mizuoto-Sample-Rate` header is the rate and `X-Mizuoto-Job` the job (the result is still stored). Streaming text is not available this way.","locale":"en"},"7309":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-291","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"Clients written for OpenAI's speech API work with Mizuoto. The two routes are under `/v1` (not under `/api`; at `<prefix>/v1` with `--api-prefix`) and need the access token too:","locale":"en"},"7310":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-292","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"Route","locale":"en"},"7311":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-293","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7312":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-294","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"`POST /v1/audio/speech`","locale":"en"},"7313":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-295","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"Speak `input` and answer with the audio","locale":"en"},"7314":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-296","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"`GET /v1/models`","locale":"en"},"7315":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-297","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"The installed speech models (not speech recognition), and the aliases in `tts.model_aliases`","locale":"en"},"7316":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-298","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"How the fields map:","locale":"en"},"7317":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-299","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7318":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-300","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#openai-compatible-api","content":"