"content":"**`auto` binds nothing**: `attention()` reads one context variable, finds no policy and calls the site's reference (about 1 µs a call).","locale":"en"},"9764":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Otherwise the model's `AccelPolicy` is resolved when it loads (`policy_for(name, strict)`: one per value, so models share resolutions) and reported as `LoadedModelInfo.attention`. `LocalHandle` binds it for each step of a request with `RequestContext.accel` (the context variable lives in `runtime/context.py`, so binding loads no torch), so a stream suspended between steps never leaks its policy to another thread.","locale":"en"},"9765":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"A training stage binds its policy process-wide (`dispatch.PROCESS_POLICY`), because autograd runs backward passes, and gradient checkpointing's recomputed forwards, on threads of its own.","locale":"en"},"9766":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"A change applies to models loaded afterwards; a change to `engines.<id>.attention` unloads that engine.","locale":"en"},"9767":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Backend","locale":"en"},"9768":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"9769":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-102","page_id":"/en/docs/developmen