architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"numpy, torch","locale":"en"},"10125":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"More checks:","locale":"en"},"10126":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_only_core_inference_reaches_model_code`: no module of `mizuoto/core` outside `core/inference` imports the runtime, `nn`, the engines or the trainers.","locale":"en"},"10127":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_shared_modules_are_standard_library_only`: `core/codes.py`, `core/jobs/events.py`, `core/jobs/jsonl.py`, `core/remote/frames.py` and `core/inference/tasks.py` import only the standard library (and each other). The runtime, the engines and the training stages share them.","locale":"en"},"10128":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`check_native_package`, which each gated package's `test_<id>_package.py` calls for itself: `packages/native/*/mizuoto_*` follow the engines' rule (and may import their own package), leave the process state alone and compute attention only through `mizuoto.runtime.accel`.","locale":"en"},"10129":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_engines_import_no_other_engine`: `mizuoto/engines/<a>` never imports `mizuoto/engines/<b>`; what two engines share belongs in `nn` or `runtime`.","locale":"en"},"10130":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_native_code_leaves_global_state_alone`: no call that changes process-wide state in `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, the engines and the gated packages (see Runtime).","locale":"en"},"10131":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_attention_goes_through_the_accel_entry_point`: outside `runtime/accel`, the runtime, `nn`, the engines, the trainers and the gated packages never call SDPA or its aten kernels directly; every attention computation goes through `accel.attention`, so `compute.attention` can switch it (see Attention acceleration).","locale":"en"},"10132":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_host_never_imports_model_code`: nothing in `core`, `api` or `cli` imports torch, torchaudio, transformers, onnxruntime, `mizuoto_fishspeech` or `mizuoto_indextts`, even inside a function.","locale":"en"},"10133":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Three subprocess tests: `import mizuoto.core.context` loads neither torch, fastapi nor typer; `import mizuoto.cli.app` loads neither torch nor fastapi; importing the engine contract, the request context, the dummy engine, `core.inference.local` and `core.inference.runtime` loads no torch. That keeps `mizuoto version` and `mizuoto --help` fast and lets the core's tests run on the dummy engine.","locale":"en"},"10134":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"`test_one_distribution`: `pyproject.toml` depends on torch and on no other `mizuoto-*` distribution, and `packages/` holds no worker package and no engine packages besides `packages/native`.","locale":"en"},"10135":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"Each rule has a reason:","locale":"en"},"10136":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**The core does not need torch to start.** Listing models, editing settings or serving the UI never loads a model; the runtime is built the first time a model loads.","locale":"en"},"10137":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-58","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**`core/inference` is the one door**, so the core's knowledge of model code sits in one package, and every import of it is visibly lazy.","locale":"en"},"10138":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-59","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**The shared modules are standard library only**, because a training stage, the remote agent's frames and the engines all use them without the core's pydantic models.","locale":"en"},"10139":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-60","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layer-rules-and-their-tests","content":"**Engines import no other engine**: shared code goes into `nn` or `runtime`, where it is tested once.","locale":"en"},"10140":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-61","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#one-operation-one-core-method","content":"Each operation has exactly one core method, taking and returning `Record` models (`mizuoto/core/record.py`). Routes and commands parse the input, call it and shape the output. Listing presets, for example:","locale":"en"},"10141":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-62","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#one-operation-one-core-method","content":"So the API's JSON has the same shape as the CLI's `--json`. `Record` sets `json_schema_serialization_defaults_required`: defaulted fields are required in the output schema, and the generated TypeScript types match what the server sends.","locale":"en"},"10142":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-63","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`build_services()` in `mizuoto/core/context.py` builds every service in dependency order and returns the `Services` dataclass:","locale":"en"},"10143":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-64","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"10144":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-65","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Class","locale":"en"},"10145":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-66","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"Responsibility","locale":"en"},"10146":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-67","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`settings`","locale":"en"},"10147":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-68","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`SettingsService`","locale":"en"},"10148":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-69","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`settings.toml`, `MIZUOTO_` environment overrides, resolved folders","locale":"en"},"10149":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-70","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`events`","locale":"en"},"10150":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-71","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`LocalEventBus`","locale":"en"},"10151":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-72","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"In-process publish/subscribe","locale":"en"},"10152":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-73","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_services","content":"`db`","locale":"en"},"10153":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-74","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#assembly-build_servic