e built web UI inside, every engine under a permissive licence included) and the wheels of the two licence-gated engines, `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. All three install into one environment over a torch the user chose, and each is versioned, checked and released on its own. This page covers how they are built, checked and published to PyPI (with twine, by the release workflow).","locale":"en"},"11389":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#dependencies","content":"Mizuoto is one environment: the dependencies of the core, the API, the command line, the web UI and every engine are in `pyproject.toml` and install at once. Every new dependency must answer three questions: does it have wheels for every platform CI covers (Linux x86_64, Windows x86_64, macOS arm64, CPython 3.10–3.13), does it change results, does it change process-wide state.","locale":"en"},"11390":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"For","locale":"en"},"11391":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Packages","locale":"en"},"11392":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"11393":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Web and command line","locale":"en"},"11394":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"fastapi (≥ 0.115.3), starlette (≥ 0.40), uvicorn, websockets, python-socketio, pydantic 2, httpx, typer (\\< 0.28), rich, tomli-w, tomli (Python \\< 3.11), send2trash","locale":"en"},"11395":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Starlette 0.40's `FileResponse` honours Range, so the player seeks; uvicorn speaks WebSocket only with websockets installed; typer has an upper bound because the command line uses its private modules","locale":"en"},"11396":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Audio","locale":"en"},"11397":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"av (PyAV), numpy","locale":"en"},"11398":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Decoding, encoding and resampling through PyAV, the rest with numpy; no ffmpeg or sox program is called","locale":"en"},"11399":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Runtime","locale":"en"},"11400":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"torch (≥ 2.8), safetensors, soxr, tokenizers","locale":"en"},"11401":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"torch's build is the user's (below); soxr is the resampler librosa calls; tokenizers builds the BPE transformers builds","locale":"en"},"11402":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"11403":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"pypinyin, rjieba, jieba, opencc, kaldifst, inflect, tiktoken, regex, wordsegment, budoux, ToJyutping, fasttext-predict, pyyaml","locale":"en"},"11404":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Many versions are **pinned** (`pypinyin==0.55.0`, `opencc==1.4.2`, `inflect==7.3.1`…): the engines' output depends on them, and another version changes phones and audio","locale":"en"},"11405":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"The licence-gated packages bring a few of their own: `mizuoto-fishspeech` needs tokenizers and safetensors, `mizuoto-indextts` sentencepiece. Each also names the packages it imports directly that Mizuoto already brings (torch and numpy; `mizuoto-indextts` also pyyaml and tiktoken), with Mizuoto's bounds, so its dependencies do not rest on Mizuoto's.","locale":"en"},"11406":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Extra","locale":"en"},"11407":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Packages","locale":"en"},"11408":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"For","locale":"en"},"11409":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]`","locale":"en"},"11410":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`pyopenjtalk==0.4.1`","locale":"en"},"11411":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"GPT-SoVITS's Japanese front end; published as a source distribution only, so installing it needs CMake and a C++ compiler","locale":"en"},"11412":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`mizuoto[gptsovits-ko]`","locale":"en"},"11413":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`python-mecab-ko==1.3.7`, `jamo==0.4.1`","locale":"en"},"11414":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"GPT-SoVITS's Korean front end","locale":"en"},"11415":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`mizuoto-indextts[ja]`","locale":"en"},"11416":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"fugashi, unidic-lite","locale":"en"},"11417":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"IndexTTS-2.5's Japanese segmentation","locale":"en"},"11418":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Without an extra, text in that language fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint; `mizuoto doctor` lists each engine's missing extras too. The optional attention packages (flash-attn, xFormers, SageAttention) are not extras: they must match the user's torch, and `mizuoto doctor` prints install commands that keep the installed torch (`--no-deps`); see Attention acceleration.","locale":"en"},"11419":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"Every engine is ported in-tree, so none of these upstream dependencies is needed any more:","locale":"en"},"11420":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"No longer needed","locale":"en"},"11421":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"Replaced by","locale":"en"},"11422":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"vLLM, TensorRT / TensorRT-LLM, FlashInfer, flash-attn as a requirement","locale":"en"},"11423":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"Autoregressive decoding without waits and as CUDA graphs, optional `torch.compile`, SDPA and the optional attention backends","locale":"en"},"11424":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"transformers (several incompatible versions), accelerate, huggingface_hub, peft, loralib","locale":"en"},"11425":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"In-tree modules (the Qwen decoder, GPT-2, BERT, HuBERT, w2v-BERT, Whisper…), `tokenizers`, an in-tree LoRA","locale":"en"},"11426":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"onnxruntime","locale":"en"},"11427":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"The weights in ONNX files are converted into torch modules by an in-tree protobuf reader (`runtime/convert/onnx.py`), the result cached under the model folder's `.mizuoto/`","locale":"en"},"11428":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"openai-whisper, faster-whisper (CTranslate2)","locale":"en"},"11429":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"An in-tree Whisper, log-mel and the `tiktoken` vocabulary (shipped)","locale":"en"},"11430":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"torchaudio, librosa, numba, resampy, scipy","locale":"en"},"11431":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"`mizuoto.nn.dsp`, bit-exact with those libraries; soxr","locale":"en"},"11432":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"descript-audiotools, descript-audio-codec","locale":"en"},"11433":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-58","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"`mizuoto/nn/codecs/dac.py`","locale":"en"},"11434":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-59","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"pynini, WeTextProcessing, wetext, modelscope","locale":"en"},"11435":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-60","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"kaldifst with exported FSTs (shared assets, or shipped in the package)","locale":"en"},"11436":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-61","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"jieba_fast, g2p_en, nltk (and the data it downloads at run time)","locale":"en"},"11437":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-62","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"jieba; the ported GRU and tagger, with their data shipped","locale":"en"},"11438":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-63","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"hyperpyyaml, omegaconf, hydra","locale":"en"},"11439":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-64","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"YAML read as data, and dataclass configs","locale":"en"},"11440":{"id":"/en/docs/development-rele