10403,"Adding things"],[9813,"additive bias; causal and local masks"],[7038,"Address"],[7428,"Address"],[9111,"Address to bind"],[9203,"Address to bind; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[9065,"Address to listen on (default from settings: `127.0.0.1`; `0.0.0.0` for every interface)"],[8409,"Address to listen on; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[7019,"Addresses and documentation"],[11007,"Adds"],[9887,"After a capture the current stream waits for the capture stream: beginning a capture resets the generator's seed and offset tensors on the capture stream, and a first replay that overtook those kernels would draw from offset 0."],[11599,"After a load; when the model is unloaded (frees without copying back)"],[13466,"After a model change the screen picks a suitable way: the library voice you had chosen when it suits the new model, else a preset speaker, a description or a clip, in that order."],[10754,"After adding or changing a model, run `python scripts/dev.py model-manifests omnivoice`. `scripts/model_manifests.py` pins the Hugging Face revision to the current commit and lists every file with its size and SHA-256 (LFS files from their metadata, small files fetched and hashed) into `manifests/files/<manifest>`. Downloads verify against it; `test_catalogue_models_have_files_manifests` checks that every catalogue model has one."],[13672,"After confirming, runs every stage again from the first"],[7553,"After Hugging Face, also upload to ModelScope with `modelscope upload`"],[8294,"after that, allow a cheaper way for the step (tiled decoding, smaller batches): it fits in less memory, and its output differs slightly and says so"],[1425,"agent 使用 TLS"],[1484,"agent 使用自签名证书时，在主机上用 `--ca-file` 给出这份证书；这种情况下不检查证书中的主机名。不给 `--ca-file` 时使用系统的 CA。"],[1410,"agent 使用这台机器自己的数据文件夹（设置、模型、缓存），和这台机器上的 `mizuoto webui` 一样；要让它用另一个文件夹，设置环境变量 `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR`。引擎运行在 agent 自己的进程里。"],[1414,"agent 在前台运行，直到 Ctrl+C。它自己的空闲卸载、显存处理等遵循那台机器的设置（`compute.*`、`engines.<id>.*`）。端口被占用时启动失败，提示换一个 `--port`。"],[4670,"agent 对每个操作先回 `progress`、`chunk`（二进制帧：float32 小端单声道）和 `file` 帧，最后是 `result` 或 `error`，并每 5 秒发一次心跳。超过 `remote.heartbeat_timeout`（60 秒）收不到任何帧，主机就以 `worker_failed`（`during = \"heartbeat\"`）关闭会话；下一个请求重新连接。"],[1481,"agent 工作时每 5 秒发一次心跳；超过这个时间没有任何消息，请求失败"],[392,"agent 有自己的数据卷和模型；它的镜像与主机的镜像构建方式相同（相同的 Mizuoto 版本，要提供需许可的引擎时用 `GATED=1`）。镜像的健康检查请求的是网页界面的 7869 端口，agent 不提供它，所以这里用 `--no-healthcheck` 关掉。agent 没有 TLS 时请求和音频以明文传输，请只在可信的网络中使用，或用 `--ssl-certfile` / `--ssl-keyfile` 提供证书（把证书文件挂载进容器）。"],[2523,"agent 的 `host:port`（端口默认 7870）"],[1421,"agent 的 `host` 或 `host:port`（端口默认 7870），IPv6 写作 `[::1]:7870`"],[2544,"agent 的 TLS 证书"],[1423,"agent 的令牌。修改已有主机时不给出则保留原来的令牌"],[2526,"agent 的令牌（那台机器上的 `remote.agent.token`）"],[2538,"agent 端口"],[1359,"agent：提供引擎的机器"],[12698,"Alibaba Qwen's 12 Hz speech language model (QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS, Apache-2.0). Code: `mizuoto/engines/qwen3tts`. On the CPU in fp32 with the same seed it gives the audio of Mizuoto 0.1 (upstream's `qwen_tts` behind its adapter) sample for sample, in all eight parity cases, and its trainer gives 0.1's checkpoint byte for byte. What each variant offers is in Engines in depth."],[7864,"Alibaba Qwen's 12 Hz speech LLM. Best for: high-quality cloning in ten languages, preset speakers steered by instructions (emotion, pace, style), and new voices from a one-sentence description."],[12269,"Alibaba Tongyi's LLM + flow-matching TTS (QwenAudio/CosyVoice, Apache-2.0). Code: `mizuoto/engines/cosyvoice`. Given the same voice prompt it is identical to upstream (on torch 2.8) sample for sample on the CPU, for every model and mode; through the whole stack, where each side makes its own voice prompt, it agrees to 23–68 dB SNR, for reasons explained below. Its trainers give upstream's checkpoints byte for byte. User-facing details: Engines in depth."],[7900,"Alibaba Tongyi's LLM + flow-matching TTS. Best for: low-latency token-level streaming, speaking text as it is written (streamed text input), converting a recording to another voice, and instructions for dialects, emotions and speed."],[9775,"all"],[9776,"all"],[9781,"all"],[9782,"all"],[12977,"all"],[11460,"All"],[12759,"All eight stack cases are identical to 0.1 sample for sample on the CPU in fp32: a preset speaker, an instruction, voice design, in-context cloning, x-vector cloning, a transcript from speech recognition, a dialect speaker and the fine-tuned model. Two more cases speak each implementation's training export with the other implementation; both identical. The tokenizer gives transformers' ids on the tokenizer corpus. The contract suite passes (24 tests). CUDA graphs were checked against the eager path on a GPU with a tiny model and the real 0.6B Base."],[9145,"All settings"],[12383,"All three clone (the reference's transcript is required) and edit speech. The model folder holds the checkpoint (`*.safetensors`, else `*.pt`), `vocab.txt` and `vocos/config.yaml` + `vocos/pytorch_model.bin`. E2's repository has no vocabulary, so upstream's bundled `vocab.txt` ships with the engine as package data and serves it."],[11016,"also AdamW's state in RAM, stepped on the CPU (`host_optimizer`; Qwen3-TTS, OmniVoice, F5-TTS without a gradient scaler); VoxCPM's LoRA base weights streamed from RAM for each product (`streamed_linear`)"],[8654,"Also copy the result here"],[8671,"Also copy the result here"],[8688,"Also copy the result here"],[8588,"Also copy the result here; its extension picks the format"],[9689,"always"],[11018,"Always: a GPU stage reports `memory/peak_mb`; `MethodInfo.memory_mb` estimates a run's peak per preset from the model's size, and a GPU run warns in its log, naming the preset that would fit, when the estimate exceeds the free memory. Trainers themselves are in Trainers."],[11453,"AMD (ROCm; `cuda` to torch)"],[6996,"AMD、Intel、Apple 芯片和纯 CPU 的 torch 构建，以及从源码或用 Docker 安装，见安装。"],[4437,"AMD（ROCm，torch 里也叫 `cuda`）"],[13561,"An **experiment**: a model to start from and a way to train it, run on the dataset stage by stage with the engine's own fine-tuning recipe, implemented in Mizuoto. The result is **a voice's own weights** (added to a voice in the library) or **a new model** (listed under **Models**)."],[10446,"An `EventBase` subclass (`__event_name__`) in `core/events/models.py`; it enters the OpenAPI schema by itself. Regenerate the types and handle it in the UI's `api/socket.ts`"],[7347,"An agent in a container"],[10491,"An AI image browser on the same skeleton"],[9967,"An API that can delete and move files checks three things on every HTTP and WebSocket request (before any route; plain ASGI):"],[9719,"An architecture test forbids `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` and its aten kernels anywhere outside `runtime/accel/`."],[8697,"An audio file"],[9883,"An autoregressive model on a GPU launches thousands of small kernels per step (Qwen3-TTS: about 6 000 per 80 ms frame), and every wait for the device drains the queue, so the CPU's launch time and the GPU's work add up instead of overlapping. Each decoder now waits for the device once per frame or token, and with `compute.cuda_graphs` (on by default; NVIDIA only, ROCm's HIP graphs unchecked) its step's kernels are captured once and replayed at once. A graph replays exactly the kernels the eager code launched, with the same arguments, so its results are the eager code's bit for bit."],[12039,"An effective hyperparameter, `default` when `None`"],[8606,"An emotion weight `name=value` (repeatable)"],[10237,"An engine has two parts: a **manifest** (`mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/<id>.toml`, package data shipped in the wheel) and an **implementation** (a subclass of `mizuoto.runtime.engine.Engine`)."],[10710,"An engine in Mizuoto is two things in two places, plus its tests:"],[10818,"An engine is *available* when torch imports (the dummy engine needs none) and its implementation is registered; otherwise `EngineStatus.missing` names what is missing and the UI and `mizuoto doctor` show the fix."],[10759,"An engine is a package under `mizuoto/engines/<id>/` whose `__init__.py` exports the `Engine` subclass, and whose modules import only what the layer rules allow: `mizuoto.runtime`, `mizuoto.nn`, `mizuoto.text`, `mizuoto.training`, `mizuoto.core.codes`, `mizuoto.core.inference.tasks`, its own package, and numpy, torch and the text libraries; never another engine. Its module imports no torch at the top (`test_engine_contract_import_is_light` and `test_manifest_options_match_the_engines` import engine modules without torch): torch is imported inside the methods, and type hints go under `if TYPE_CHECKING:`."],[10938,"An engine marks submodules on the handle with `handle.mark(module, mark)`:"],[8157,"An engine needs torch (only the dummy engine runs without it) and its implementation: every engine is built into Mizuoto except Fish Speech and IndexTTS, which are distributions of their own. The engine card and `mizuoto doctor <engine>` say what is missing:"],[8459,"An engine on a remote host is marked **On gpu-box** (the host's name) on its engine card and model rows, with the hints **Its packages are gpu-box’s: mizuoto doctor qwen3tts there** for the engine and **These are the models on gpu-box: download them there with mizuoto model download** for its models."],[10449,"An engine option"],[8614,"An engine option `name=value` (repeatable)"],[10453,"An engine or a trainer"],[7172,"An engine raised an exception"],[10798,"An engine returns float32 mono audio in `[-1, 1]` at the model's own rate and never encodes: joining, normalising, resampling and encoding are the core's job. It receives resolved, absolute paths that exist (references are 16-bit WAV in `cache/refs/`) and never downloads. The core has validated the request against the manifest, so an engine maps rather than checks."],[8257,"An engine serves one request at a time on a device; the next waits (**Waiting for the engine**). A job waiting for a GPU another job holds shows **Waiting for the GPU**; when the memory suffices for both, **Run anyway** in **Jobs** starts it beside the other, or raise `compute.gpu_jobs`. A fine-tune takes the whole GPU, whatever `compute.gpu_jobs` says, and the idle models on it move to RAM first."],[10251,"An engine whose device is `<host>/<device>` runs on that host's `mizuoto agent`. The agent is a whole Mizuoto: its own data folder, models and engines, in its own process."],[10903,"An engine with `PHASED = True` (every real engine Mizuoto ships; the dummy is not) wraps each part of a request in a phase, so only that part's components are placed, with that part's working memory set aside:"],[10907,"An engine without `PHASED` gets every handle for the whole call, with `memory_required(task)` as the working memory."],[11592,"An engine's `DEVICES` (every kind by default) mirror its manifest's `devices`; `torch.compile` runs eagerly on MPS."],[10241,"An engine's `OPTION_SCHEMA` must equal its manifest's `[options]`, and `Engine.DEVICES` its manifest's `devices` (`tests/core/test_engines.py` checks both); the engine's `detect_variant()` (files only, no torch) gives the same variant as `core/models/detect.py`, which the host uses when importing a model."],[8892,"An engine's variants, capabilities, parameters and models"],[7119,"An error answers with its HTTP status and one shape:"],[10445,"An event"],[13169,"An example:"],[12014,"An experiment is `experiments/<engine>/<name>/`: `experiment.json` (base model, dataset, method, hyperparameters, stage states), the trainer's work folder `work/`, and `metrics.jsonl`."],[8998,"An experiment is named `<engine>/<name>`, or just its name when that is unique."],[13663,"An experiment is saved in `experiments/<engine>/<name>/`."],[13150,"An imported script is plain text, with these rules (the hint under the box says the same):"],[11429,"An in-tree Whisper, log-mel and the `tiktoken` vocabulary (shipped)"],[8112,"An internal engine Mizuoto uses itself: Whisper large-v3-turbo, implemented in Mizuoto, about 100 languages, transcribing reference clips, voices and