4027,"Downloads are jobs: you can leave the page and follow them under **Jobs** at the top right. The first synthesis loads the model; the next ones are much faster."],[7584,"Downloads then try this server first; files it lacks (and official repository files the custom address does not serve) come from Hugging Face, hf-mirror and ModelScope in turn. `check --endpoint http://192.168.1.10:8000 --repo team/mizuoto-model` tells whether the mirror is complete."],[7475,"Downloads use httpx, which reads the standard proxy variables `HTTPS_PROXY`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY`. Set them in the environment that starts `mizuoto webui` or `mizuoto model download`."],[9932,"Draw with `multinomial1` / `multinomial_draws` and keep decoding steps free of waits (no `.item()`, `tolist()`, Python scalars into tensors, masked assignment) except one per step."],[13468,"Drop audio on **Drop audio files here**, or click it to choose a file (WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG…). Or:"],[10797,"Drop the weights (the manager has already taken the handles off their devices)"],[11867,"DSP, samplers, tokenizers, normalisers, g2p"],[12919,"DSP, samplers, tokenizers, normalisers, g2p"],[5903,"DSP、采样器、分词器、文本规范化、g2p"],[4851,"DSP、采样器、分词器、规范化器、字音转换"],[9770,"dtypes"],[4989,"dummy"],[12005,"dummy"],[4755,"dummy 引擎"],[10611,"E.g. CosyVoice-BlankEN's weights and the semantic codec IndexTTS-2.5 never reads only took space"],[954,"E2-TTS Base"],[7970,"E2-TTS Base"],[5366,"E2-TTS 的 UNetT：带跳连的扁平 transformer，x-transformers 的 RMSNorm"],[12382,"E2-TTS's UNetT: a flat transformer with skip connections, x-transformers' RMSNorm"],[11679,"Each `LocalEngine` is a memory holder: **Free GPU memory** (`POST /api/v1/compute/release`) unloads every model of every idle holder and offloads what is left; refused while a holder is busy"],[12716,"Each 80 ms frame of audio is 16 codes. The **talker**, a 28-layer Qwen3 decoder over text and codec embeddings, predicts the frame's first code; the **code predictor**, a 5-layer transformer, predicts the other 15 one after the other; the sum of the 16 code embeddings (plus the next text token's embedding) is the talker's next input. The **12 Hz codec** turns codes back into 24 kHz audio (1920 samples a frame) and, for cloning, the reference into codes. Base models also have a **speaker encoder** (ECAPA-TDNN) whose embedding sits in the prompt."],[11215,"Each autoregressive decoder launched thousands of small kernels per step one by one and waited for the device many times a step (`torch.multinomial`'s checks, masks copied at each step, padding masks read back, stop checks), so the CPU's launch time and the GPU's work added up. Each now waits once per step and, with `compute.cuda_graphs`, replays its step's kernels as CUDA graphs (Acceleration). Every result below is the old code's audio or tokens; the CPU parity cases of each engine stayed identical. All on the shared GPUs described above."],[11621,"Each call to an engine gets one `RequestContext` (`mizuoto/runtime/context.py`):"],[13714,"Each clip gets a **What is said in the clip** field. It may stay empty: **Missing transcripts are filled by speech recognition when it is installed.**"],[13630,"Each clip’s peak at -1 dBFS"],[10064,"Each command is a plain function, its parameters declared with `Annotated[..., typer.Option(...)]`"],[8498,"Each connection starts with the token, which the agent compares in constant time; a wrong one closes the connection."],[11463,"Each distribution has a version of its own, in a file that holds nothing else; a push to `main` that changes it releases that distribution (see below):"],[10580,"Each distribution has its own version and is checked and released on its own; a gated package names the Mizuoto versions it works with (`mizuoto>=0.2.0,<0.3`)"],[8180,"Each engine's licence is in Engines in depth."],[10271,"Each event in `mizuoto/core/events/models.py` is a `Record` with an `__event_name__`: `job_updated`, `job_log`, `jobs_cleared`, `outputs_added` / `outputs_removed`, `voices_changed`, `models_changed`, `presets_changed`, `engines_changed`, `runtime_changed` (the loaded models and the engines' states, as `RuntimeStatus`), `compute_changed`, `settings_changed`, `datasets_changed`, `projects_changed`, `experiments_changed`, `train_metrics`. `EventBase.get_events()` collects every subclass; `mizuoto/api/openapi.py` writes them into the OpenAPI schema, from which the UI types its socket."],[7536,"Each file goes where Mizuoto's mirror source asks for it. A copy in a models folder with the same size and SHA-256 is hard-linked (else copied); anything else is downloaded from the official sources by Mizuoto's own downloader: resumed, retried and checked against its SHA-256."],[7444,"Each file picks its source on its own:"],[12015,"Each finished stage records a fingerprint, computed by `fingerprints()` and chained in stage order:"],[13338,"Each host shows its state (**Online**, **Offline**, **Refused**), **Devices**, **Installed engines** and **Used by**, and can be changed or removed. **Check again** refreshes every host."],[8448,"Each host shows its state (**Online**, **Offline**, **Refused**), **Devices**, **Installed engines** and **Used by**; **Check again** reconnects at once."],[8505,"Each host's state (`refresh` reconnects)"],[13738,"Each installed model, and whether and how it can use the voice: **Clone**, **Clone (no transcript)**, **Preset speaker**, **Designed** or **Trained**, with badges such as **own weights**, **transcribed first** or **trimmed to fit**; models that cannot say why."],[13141,"Each line is rendered on its own, and each rendering is a **take**. After you change a line's text, speaker or settings, only that line needs rendering again; at the end the lines are joined, with the pauses you set, into one file with subtitles. Speakers may use models of different engines."],[10434,"Each Mizuoto engine is a port of an upstream project and must give **the same** results: on the CPU in fp32 with the same seed, the audio is identical sample for sample (for trainers: losses, learning rates and saved weights identical byte for byte). This rule decides much of how code is written:"],[8337,"each model as its original implementation did, so results stay identical to it"],[11871,"Each module with real weights on captured inputs"],[12922,"each module with the real weights on captured inputs"],[10689,"Each needs its own hint and exit code"],[10140,"Each operation has exactly one core method, taking and returning `Record` models (`mizuoto/core/record.py`). Routes and commands parse the input, call it and shape the output. Listing presets, for example:"],[7109,"Each operation is one method of the core; the API and the command line only parse, call it and print the result. So the `mizuoto … --json` of a listing or a query prints the JSON its route returns, for example `mizuoto model list --json` and `GET /api/v1/models`. The exception is `mizuoto speak --json`, which prints `{\"job\": …, \"outputs\": […]}`: the job plus the output records."],[9847,"Each optional backend imports its package the first time a policy asks for it on a device, then checks it:"],[11919,"each package in scope × Ubuntu, Windows, macOS × Python 3.10, 3.13"],[11922,"each package in scope, Ubuntu, Python 3.12"],[10596,"Each port matches its reference sample for sample (CPU, fp32, same seed); the reference is how Mizuoto 0.1 actually called upstream, not upstream's demos"],[13238,"Each rendering of a line adds a take and uses it at once. Up to 5 takes are kept per line; older ones not in use are deleted. **Take N** in the line's menu goes back to an earlier one."],[7190,"Each request passes three checks (`mizuoto/api/security.py`):"],[13033,"Each result"],[12159,"Each route's `meta.screen` in `router.ts` names the navigation destination it belongs to; `addressOf(screen)` remembers each destination's last address, so the navigation goes back to the voice or project it left rather than to the list."],[13121,"Each row shows the name, size, description and **used by** *models*. Each can be downloaded or deleted on its own. A model missing a shared file it needs shows as **Partly downloaded**. Shared files are kept in `models/_assets/<engine>/` in the data folder."],[10135,"Each rule has a reason:"],[13043,"Each shows its text (or name), length, waveform (click to seek), model, time taken, real-time factor (RTF) and seed, with any warnings and licence notices (such as Fish Speech's \"Built with Fish Audio\"). Its menu:"],[12757,"Each training forward gets a fresh cache: the first `DynamicCache` update concatenates, so attention sees contiguous keys and values, as upstream's."],[13710,"Each voice is a folder under `voices/<name>/` in the data folder (`voice.json` and FLAC clips in `references/`). The list is a scan of those folders, so a voice folder copied in appears too."],[12728,"ECAPA-TDNN as Qwen2.5-Omni ships it: no BatchNorm, reflection padding, a 128-bin log-mel at 24 kHz in, a 2048-wide embedding out"],[13520,"Edit speech"],[13550,"Editing clips"],[13128,"Editing the script"],[7363,"Effect"],[7383,"Effect"],[9855,"Effect"],[7595,"Embedding the server"],[13483,"Emotion (IndexTTS-2 and 2.5) comes three ways, as the model supports:"],[12577,"Emotion from a clip, from eight weights, or from a description"],[13873,"emotion from weights, a clip or a description"],[8226,"empty"],[8245,"empty"],[8278,"empty"],[9384,"empty"],[9408,"empty"],[9541,"empty"],[9547,"empty"],[9263,"empty (`cache/`)"],[9251,"empty (`datasets/`)"],[9255,"empty (`experiments/`)"],[9239,"empty (`models/`)"],[9247,"empty (`outputs/`)"],[9259,"empty (`projects/`)"],[9243,"empty (`voices/`)"],[8903,"Enable or disable an engine (`engine disable {engine_id}` keeps its models installed)."],[7828,"Engine"],[8316,"Engine"],[9865,"Engine"],[9893,"Engine"],[10978,"Engine"],[11350,"Engine"],[11973,"Engine"],[12859,"Engine"],[13107,"Engine"],[13563,"Engine"],[13831,"Engine"],[7756,"Engine (id)"],[12073,"Engine availability"],[10163,"Engine manifests (`core/engines/manifests/*.toml`), licence acceptance, each engine's availability"],[11800,"Engine options make it misbehave on purpose: `delay_ms`, `chunk_ms` and `load_delay_ms` slow it down; `fail = error | oom | crash | exception` and `fail_at_segment` make it fail, run out of memory, report a crash (`worker_failed`) or raise an unhandled exception where asked."],[12845,"Engine reference"],[7068,"Engine state (available or what is missing) and configuration, licences, one engine's checks"],[9475,"Engine-specific load options (CosyVoice's `fp16`, IndexTTS's `use_qwen_emo`…); see Engines in depth"],[7220,"Engine-specific operations (their payload may name server files)"],[7257,"Engine-specific options"],[10749,"Engine-specific options (`engine_options`); unknown ones always raise; `group = \"hidden\"` keeps one out of forms. The engine's `OPTION_SCHEMA` must mirror them exactly"],[11063,"Engine, case"],[11135,"Engine, case"],[11178,"Engine, recipe"],[50,"engines"],[7066,"engines"],[7852,"Engines"],[12947,"Engines"],[13066,"Engines"],[13793,"Engines"],[10480,"Engines and exactness"],[8547,"Engines and the runtime"],[13337,"Engines can run on other machines: run `mizuoto agent` there (it has its own engines and models), add it here, then choose it as an engine's device under **Models › Engines**. Training stays on this machine."],[10674,"Engines get references as `cache/refs/<sha256>.wav` (16-bit WAV); voices store FLAC"],[10421,"Engines import only `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, `training`, `core.codes`, `core.inference.tasks` and their own package, and **never another engine**. Code two engines share goes into `nn` or `runtime`."],[7739,"Engines in depth"],[11647,"Engines share one process with the server, each other and the tests, so native code **changes nothing process-wide**. `test_native_code_leaves_global_state_alone` forbids, in `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, the engines and the gated packages:"],[10424,"Engines, trainers, the runtime and the server share one process, so code under `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, `engines` and `packages/native` keeps these rules (details in Runtime):"],[9280,"Engines' default device: `auto`, `cpu`, `cuda:N` (NVIDIA, or AMD on ROCm), `xpu:N` (Intel) or `mps`"],[10203,"Entry"],[10817,"Entry points are read once per process: installing such a distribution means restarting Mizuoto. Its package follows the engines' rules and mirrors its manifest (`check_native_package`, `check_options_mirror`, called by its `tests/test_<id>_package.py`), has its own version in `mizuoto_<id>/version.py` with the Mizuoto versions it works with in its `pyproject.toml` (`check_gated_distribution`), is checked by CI's `gated` and `oldest-mizuoto` jobs and is built by `scripts/build_wheels.py native` (see Release)."],[11913,"Environment"],[10479,"Environment and distribution"],[9144,"Environment variables"],[9159,"environment variables `MIZUOTO_<GROUP>__<FIELD>`;"],[9161,"Environment variables and pinned values live in memory only: they are **never written back** to `settings.toml` and cannot be changed in the web UI or through the API. The web UI marks a setting an environment variable overrides **Set by an environment variable**, and one the embedding application pins **Set by the application Mizuoto runs in**; `mizuoto config set` on a setting an environment variable overrides says `An environment variable overrides this setting.`."],[10258,"Environment variables with the `MIZUOTO_` prefix and `__` between levels override the file, e.g. `MIZUOTO_SERVER__PORT=8000`. `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` and `MIZUOTO_CONFIG_DIR` are the exceptions: they choose folders."],[7380,"Environment variables:"],[8462,"Error"],[9604,"Error code"],[7023,"Errors"],[7594,"Errors"],[10705,"Errors"],[11548,"Errors"],[9941,"Errors → HTTP: `errors.py`"],[10095,"Errors and exit codes"],[10073,"Errors: `DebugTyperCommand.invoke` catches `MizuotoError`; `report_error()` prints the message, and the fixing command when `detail[\"hint\"]` has one, then exits with the error's `exit_code`. Heavy modules (core models, uvicorn) are imported inside functions: `tests/test_architecture.py` checks that importing `mizuoto.cli.app` loads neither torch nor fastapi."],[7268,"Event"],[7030,"Events"],[7593,"Events"],[10092,"Events"],[7045,"Events (socket.io)"],[7703,"Every API and socket request must carry it; the web UI asks for it once"],[9716,"Every attention computation in `runtime`, `nn`, the engines, the trainers and the gated packages goes through one entry point, after ComfyUI's attention backends and `comfy_kitchen`'s registry:"],[8333,"Every attention computation of every engine and trainer goes through one switch, `compute.attention` (**Settings** › **Compute** › **Attention**), after ComfyUI's attention backends:"],[13002,"Every catalogue model with its engine, size, GPU memory and state, and a **Download** button; see Downloading models"],[13182,"Every change is saved a moment after you stop typing, and when you leave the page; there is nothing to save by hand."],[12084,"Every colour role (`primary`, `on-primary`, `surface-container`, `outline`…) generated from one seed colour with `@material/material-color-utilities`' Tonal Spot scheme, light and dark, at contrast 0 (standard), 0.5 (medium) and 1 (high)"],[8572,"Every command takes these options; the tables leave them out:"],[9972,"Every core error (`mizuoto/core/errors.py`) carries `code`, `http_status` and `exit_code`; `install_error_handlers()` turns any `MizuotoError` into one shape:"],[11824,"Every declared voice mode, in English and Chinese, is audible (RMS > 0.01), at the right rate, about as long as the text needs; with ASR installed, word error rate \\< 0.35"],[12930,"Every engine above is identical at T3, with no error at all, except CosyVoice when each side makes its own voice prompt. Two opt-in paths are held to less: `compute.compile` (within 1e-4, except CosyVoice, whose vocoder amplifies float differences) and Qwen3-TTS's `fused_projections` (identical on the CPU, not on a GPU)."],[13682,"Every engine also trains on a CPU, which is enough to check the whole run works with little data and few steps."],[8361,"Every engine and every trainer runs on a CPU, which is fine for trying things and short sentences, but much slower than a GPU, especially for long texts and training (GPT-SoVITS trains in minutes on a GPU and hours on a CPU). Smaller models (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, GPT-SoVITS) shorten the wait noticeably; `compute.compile` helps F5-TTS most."],[9681,"Every engine gives its upstream's output sample for sample on the CPU (see Engines in depth), and speed work keeps it that way: **a default never changes a result**. Faster paths that compute the same kernels with the same arguments (CUDA graphs, fewer waits for the device, CPU memory and thread placement) are on by default. Faster paths that change the arithmetic (other attention kernels, TF32, `torch.compile`, fused projections) are opt-in, and every output lists the ones that ran. Measurements are in Performance record; GPU memory is in Memory."],[12857,"Every engine in Mizuoto is a port: the model code of an upstream project, written again on Mizuoto's runtime (`mizuoto/runtime`) and its shared building blocks (`mizuoto/nn`, `mizuoto/text`). No upstream code is vendored, and no engine imports transformers, onnxruntime or the upstream package. Each port is held to one standard: on the CPU, in fp32, with the same seed, it gives the output of the code it replaces, sample for sample."],[11762,"Every engine is already installed with Mizuoto; a real one needs only its models:"],[7827,"Every engine is implemented in Mizuoto and runs in the server's own process, in the one Python environment Mizuoto is installed in. An engine is **available** when torch imports there and its implementation is installed; `mizuoto doctor` (and **Models** › **Engines**) says which engines are available and, for the others, what is missing and the command that installs it."],[13796,"Every engine is implemented in Mizuoto itself, on its own runtime over torch, and runs inside the server's process; there is one Python environment and nothing to build per engine. Requests, voices, parameters, jobs and results look the same whichever engine serves them."],[12140,"Every engine is installed with Mizuoto, but one can still be *missing* something: torch, or a licence-gated engine's own distribution. The engine list (`EngineStatus.available`, `missing`) and the doctor's report (`useDoctor(engine)` in `api/queries/engines.ts`: `GET /api/v1/engines/{id}/doctor`, or `GET /api/v1/runtime/doctor` for all) drive what the UI offers:"],[13005,"Every engine is part of Mizuoto and runs in the server's own process: there is nothing to install per engine. An engine is **Available** when torch is installed (the dummy engine needs none) and its implementation is there: built in, or for Fish Speech and IndexTTS their own distribution (`mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`). Otherwise its card under **Models › Engines** says **Not available** and what it needs, and the model picker marks its models **Not available**."],[11419,"Every engine is ported in-tree, so none of these upstream dependencies is needed any more:"],[10675,"Every engine reads 16-bit WAV; registering by content avoids duplicates"],[11552,"Every engine runs in the server's own process (or in the command's, on the command line), on Mizuoto's own runtime: `mizuoto/runtime/`, a small framework in the manner of ComfyUI's model management. The core reaches it only through `mizuoto/core/inference/`. This page covers both sides: what an engine gets from the runtime, and how the core calls a loaded model. How to write an engine is in Adding an engine."],[8215,"Every engine runs in the server's own process, on Mizuoto's runtime (torch). The defaults run on any machine. This page covers the settings that decide where models run and how long they stay loaded, the speed-ups you can turn on (attention backends, `compute.fast`, `compute.compile`), and how waiting requests are batched. The defaults keep every result identical to each engine's original implementation; each opt-in that changes results says so. Each engine is described in Engines in depth; every setting is listed in Configuration."],[7850,"Every engine runs on a CPU too, much more slowly. The speed-up option is `compute.compile`, in Performance."],[8171,"Every engine runs on a CPU, much more slowly than on a GPU: the CPU runs in fp32, and large models such as Fish Speech are especially slow. Pick smaller models (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, the GPT-SoVITS v2 family…), run the engine on a GPU machine as a remote host, or turn on streaming playback to hear the audio as it is made."],[8232,"Every engine runs on NVIDIA (CUDA), AMD (ROCm), Intel (XPU) and Apple (MPS) GPUs and on the CPU. On a GPU without double precision (Apple's, and Intel Arc cards), the one model part that computes in double precision, CosyVoice 3's pitch predictor, runs on the CPU while the rest of the model stays on the GPU. On Apple silicon `compute.compile` is ignored and torch's MPS backend may lack an operation an engine needs; starting Mizuoto with `PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1` runs such operations on the CPU. The ROCm, XPU and MPS paths are not yet tested on real hardware: please report what fails."],[11488,"every engine's implementation and trainer imported (`get_engine`), every module of `mizuoto` and the gated packages imported, and every data file the checkout has beside the code of the distributions built from it found installed (the ones engines read at run time actually read);"],[10643,"Every engine's models share one process and its memory"],[10273,"Every long operation is a job. Services register a factory with `jobs.register(kind, factory)` when they are built; the factory turns a request (plain JSON) into a `JobSpec`:"],[8525,"Every mizuoto command group and command, grouped by purpose: what it does, its main arguments and options, and an example, taken from each command's --help."],[7426,"Every model in the catalogue names its repository and a pinned files manifest (`mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/files/*.files.json`): the repository's commit and each file's path, size and SHA-256. Mizuoto fetches only the listed files and checks each one's size and SHA-256, so the files are identical whichever source served them."],[10810,"Every module with weights is wrapped in a `ModelHandle` and listed in `self.handles`, so the model manager can place it, offload it and report its size:"],[7525,"every one"],[10996,"Every output's `meta.memory`: `streamed_mb` (copied from RAM during the request), `loaded_mb`, `size_mb`, and for partly loaded components `partial`: per component the `reason` (the budget fell short, `vram_mode low` or `none`, capped after running out of memory, or gave up memory for another), the `mode`, `free_mb`, `working_mb` and `reserve_mb` weighed, `loaded_mb`, `size_mb` and `gave_up_for`. The log says the same when it happens."],[10887,"Every registered component, the budget, eviction, partial loading, the OOM retry's clean-up, calibration, reporting"],[10587,"Every required dependency has wheels on every platform CI covers; without an extra, text in that language fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command"],[7053,"Every REST route is under `/api/v1`:"],[13770,"Every result"],[13823,"Every result: search, favourites, download, run again with the same settings."],[10649,"Every site passes `is_causal` as upstream did, and CosyVoice's streamed-text steps rely on the top-left form; the only site with dropout (GPT-SoVITS's T2S training) calls SDPA's own"],[12685,"Every step is a full forward of the conditional and unconditional rows over the whole sequence; there is no CUDA-graph path for this engine."],[10290,"Every synthesis job (`speak`, `convert`, `edit`), on any engine and device; a micro-batch is one job"],[10178,"Every synthesized file and its provenance"],[13258,"Every take is resampled to it (speakers' models may differ in rate)"],[11951,"Every trainable engine trains natively, in Mizuoto's own environment, on the same modules it runs inference with. Each trainer reproduces its upstream recipe: given the same seed on the CPU, its losses, learning rates and saved weights equal byte for byte those of the upstream scripts (as Mizuoto 0.1 ran them; for VoxCPM, upstream's own script). Training needs no environment and no extra of its own: trainers use the modules and dependencies inference uses, without transformers, accelerate, peft, Lightning, Hydra, datasets or webdataset. The host side is `mizuoto/core/training/service.py` (`TrainingService`); the engine side is `mizuoto/training/` (`Trainer`, `StageContext`, `stage.py`) plus each engine's trainer module. Using the Train screen is in Train."],[12909,"Every trainer gives upstream's losses, learning rates and saved weights byte for byte on the CPU when both are seeded alike, and each implementation loads the other's exports (and, but for CosyVoice's voice prompt, speaks them identically). The contract suite (the real models through the whole stack) passes for every engine on the CPU: Qwen3-TTS 24 tests, F5-TTS 12, OmniVoice 12, CosyVoice 18, Fish Speech 6, IndexTTS 18, GPT-SoVITS 24, VoxCPM 18."],[9661,"Every trainer runs in Mizuoto's own environment; each stage runs as a child process of the same Python."],[10928,"every unit streams: the fixed parts and the copies in flight only"],[13467,"Every voice in the picker carries badges saying how **this model** can use it: **Clone**, **Clone (no transcript)**, **Preset speaker**, **Designed** and so on; and when more is needed, **transcribed first** (the clip has no transcript, so it is transcribed before speaking) or **trimmed to fit** (the clip is too long and will be cut). Voices the model cannot use are greyed, with the reason. With an empty library, **New voice** is offered."],[11908,"everything"],[10679,"Everything between t