e/folder-name`."],[9764,"Otherwise the model's `AccelPolicy` is resolved when it loads (`policy_for(name, strict)`: one per value, so models share resolutions) and reported as `LoadedModelInfo.attention`. `LocalHandle` binds it for each step of a request with `RequestContext.accel` (the context variable lives in `runtime/context.py`, so binding loads no torch), so a stream suspended between steps never leaks its policy to another thread."],[9575,"Output and `--json`"],[71,"outputs"],[7087,"outputs"],[8560,"Outputs and jobs"],[8391,"Outputs, history, jobs and their logs"],[11887,"Over ≥ 20 texts × 3 voices × 3 seeds per voice per voice mode and model: mean CER/WER (Whisper large-v3-turbo) ≤ reference + 0.5 pp, and no case worse than the reference's worst + 5 pp; speaker similarity (CAM++ cosine to the reference clip) mean ≥ reference − 0.01; duration ratio within ±5 %; UTMOS mean ≥ reference − 0.05; loudness and F0 median within the reference's spread"],[9189,"Override one setting, e.g. `MIZUOTO_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `MIZUOTO_DOWNLOADS__SOURCE=hf-mirror`"],[9491,"Overrides `compute.attention` for this engine's models"],[9479,"Overrides `compute.unload_after_minutes` for this engine"],[9487,"Overrides `compute.vram_mode` for this engine's models (`auto`: the global one)"],[8246,"overrides the above for one engine"],[8513,"Overview"],[9571,"Overview"],[11391,"Packages"],[11407,"Packages"],[11711,"Packages"],[9312,"Page-locked RAM for weights that stream (MB; 0: automatic)"],[8285,"page-locked RAM for weights that stream to a GPU (faster copies; `0`: up to 40 % of RAM on Windows, more on Linux)"],[12175,"Pages"],[11532,"Pages are in `site/content/docs/`: `<slug>.mdx` in Simplified Chinese (the default language, `zh-CN`) and `<slug>.en.mdx` in English, with the same structure. The sidebars are `meta.json` and `meta.en.json`, grouped by `---Title---` separators."],[7302,"Parameter"],[7092,"Parameter presets"],[7646,"Parameter presets"],[10181,"Parameter presets"],[8915,"Parameter presets: a named set of parameters for one model, or common parameters only when no model is named."],[12775,"Parameters"],[13432,"Parameters"],[7331,"Parameters are lenient here: one the model does not take is dropped rather than refused. Errors take OpenAI's shape, `{\"error\": {\"message\", \"type\", \"param\", \"code\"}}`, with Mizuoto's error code as `code`. A successful answer carries `X-Mizuoto-Job` and `X-Mizuoto-Model` headers."],[10696,"Parameters, options and load options"],[12225,"Parity"],[12267,"Parity"],[12368,"Parity"],[12424,"Parity"],[12473,"Parity"],[12563,"Parity"],[12638,"Parity"],[12696,"Parity"],[12770,"Parity"],[11776,"Parity with the references"],[10521,"Parsing `/openapi.json` at run time into node templates"],[10711,"Part"],[10870,"Part"],[11553,"Part"],[8309,"Partly loaded models run their layers' weights through RAM each time they run: a language model pays it for every generated frame, so the more of it fits, the faster it goes. Copies overlap the computation on NVIDIA and AMD GPUs; on Intel GPUs they are synchronous."],[10965,"partly loaded ones (already slow; ComfyUI's first key);"],[10969,"Partly loading a phase's components: the smaller ones load whole first, each leaving the others at least their minimum, and the largest gets what is left, its remaining units streaming."],[10919,"partly, down to the minimum"],[10925,"partly, within that half"],[11865,"Pass"],[12917,"Passes when"],[7269,"Payload"],[11850,"Peak device memory and RAM per case, load and offload times (see Memory management)"],[9132,"PEM certificate: serve HTTPS"],[8421,"PEM certificate: serve TLS"],[9071,"PEM certificate: serve TLS (default from settings: `remote.agent.ssl_certfile`)"],[2116,"PEM 证书：以 HTTPS 提供服务"],[1405,"PEM 证书：以 TLS 提供服务"],[2055,"PEM 证书：使用 TLS（默认取自设置 `remote.agent.ssl_certfile`）"],[2211,"PEM 证书（链）：以 HTTPS 提供服务。其他电脑上的浏览器只在 HTTPS 下允许页面录音"],[12585,"Per text segment, IndexTTS-2:"],[8203,"Performance"],[11025,"Performance record"],[10854,"Phases"],[11066,"Phases (s)"],[11608,"Phases, the budget and VRAM modes, units and streaming, host copies, eviction, the exact retry, working-memory estimates and their calibration, and how an engine takes part: Memory."],[12543,"Phases: BERT around each text front-end call, HuBERT with SoVITS for the reference's semantic codes, the speaker-verification model (v2Pro), the GPT, then SoVITS (and the v4/v5 vocoder). The GPT is placed whole (its blocks read their fused projections directly; it is small, about 150 MB). A voice's own weights are switched in with `ModelHandle.replace`. The GPT's working memory is sized by the batch's longest row (its phones, the reference's codes and 16 codes a phone, within upstream's 1500 steps). With `compute.oom_fallback`, a batch that runs out of memory is spoken one text at a time."],[12451,"Phases: the codec encodes references and decodes each batch of frames; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`, the fast transformer `hot`) generates each batch, placed again as generation resumes. Each batch's working memory is the slow model's cache for its true bound: the references' codes, every text token, the frames of the batches before it and `max_new_tokens`, within `max_seq_len`. The model needs about 22 GB of GPU memory to run whole; with less, the runtime streams part of its weights."],[12340,"Phases: the frontend (speech tokenizer and CAM++) only for a voice that is not cached and for conversion; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`) makes the tokens; the flow and HiFT speak them. Streaming holds the language model and the flow together. HiFT's F0 predictor is marked `fixed` (HiFT reads its device). The language model's working memory is its cache for upstream's bound (20 speech tokens a text token after a 300-position prompt), at the KV width the model has (Qwen2's two KV heads), with one layer's copy repeated per head group, plus 512 MB. `compute.kv_cache = static` gives the Qwen2 model preallocated caches (identical on the CPU)."],[12829,"Phases: the VAE encodes a voice prompt and decodes; the model (`kind=\"sequence\"`; the local encoder and DiT `hot`, since they run many times a patch) generates; streaming holds both. If the VAE runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 latent frames."],[12622,"Phases: w2v-BERT, CAM++, the semantic codec and the regulator for a voice that is not cached (or w2v-BERT for an emotion clip); the emotion model for an emotion text; the GPT (`kind=\"sequence\"`; its GPT-2 `Conv1D` layers stream like linear layers); the s2mel; BigVGAN. A clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++. If BigVGAN runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles (IndexTTS 2/2.5). The GPT's working memory is sized by each segment: its text tokens and 24 codes a token (speech runs at about 5), within `max_mel_tokens`, for every beam, in the dtype it computes in."],[8169,"pick a smaller model (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, for one)."],[11742,"Pin the catalogue models' files (sizes, SHA-256) (`scripts/model_manifests.py`)"],[7598,"Pinned settings"],[7709,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`"],[7617,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`; never written to the file"],[13611,"Plain audio files"],[13434,"Plan, Speak and Stream"],[10677,"Planning should not wait on a model, but the result must be usable"],[10187,"Planning, `speak` / `convert` / `edit` jobs, streaming"],[11450,"Platforms"],[9671,"Policies"],[8413,"Port"],[9067,"Port (default from settings: `7870`)"],[10474,"Port selection"],[12654,"Post-processing without pydub (`Segment`: pydub's millisecond arithmetic on int16 arrays, `audioop.rms`)"],[12794,"Precision: `auto` is upstream's choice, the config's bf16 on every device including the CPU, float32 on Apple MPS; `engines.voxcpm.dtype` overrides. The VAE always runs in float32."],[9471,"Precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`"],[8230,"precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`. UI: **Precision** on the engine's card"],[