speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes)"],[9857,"TensorFloat-32 matrix products and cuDNN convolutions (NVIDIA, Ampere on)"],[2841,"TensorFloat-32 矩阵乘法和 cuDNN 卷积（NVIDIA，Ampere 及以后）"],[11819,"Test"],[12111,"Test"],[11768,"Testing"],[10720,"Tests"],[10404,"Tests a change needs"],[10212,"Tests build fully isolated services with `environ=` (instead of `os.environ`), `data_dir=` and `settings_overrides=` (`make_services` in `tests/conftest.py`). The dummy engine runs in the test's own process, as every engine does."],[11805,"Tests that need the scheduler and the reaper pass `start_background=True`. The API tests do: `create_app(make_services(start_background=True), bound_host=\"127.0.0.1\", serve_ui=False)`, then `TestClient`."],[10849,"Tests: `tests/engines_native/test_<id>_tiny.py` (an engine in its own distribution keeps them in its package's `tests/`, as `packages/native/<pkg>/tests/` do); the engine id list in `tests/core/test_engines.py::test_registry_lookups` and the `engines` override in `tests/engines/test_contract.py`."],[11402,"Text"],[13430,"Text"],[8708,"Text to look for in names, descriptions and tags (`list`)"],[12795,"Text tokens and audio patches share one sequence. Per patch, a **text-semantic language model** (MiniCPM-4 with LongRoPE and a static KV cache) and a shallower **residual acoustic language model** produce two hidden states; a **local DiT** (a bidirectional MiniCPM-4 run as a conditional flow, about 10 Euler steps with classifier-free guidance) predicts the next patch of latents from them and the previous patch; a **local encoder** embeds the patch back into the language model; a **stop head** decides whether to continue. The **AudioVAE**, a DAC-like causal convolutional codec with Snake activations, decodes the latents (v2 with sample-rate conditioning, 16 kHz latents to 48 kHz audio)."],[11801,"That is how cancellation at the next check, OOM becoming `compute_unavailable`, timeouts, unloading, the reaper and streamed chunks are all checked in seconds on a CI machine without a GPU. The dummy engine is also how users try Mizuoto out, and `smoke_wheels.py` uses it."],[10625,"That is the weights' licence; the non-commercial term is conveyed by tags and a notice"],[11900,"that package's `gated` and `oldest-mizuoto` jobs, and `torch` for it"],[9196,"The \"UI\" column names the place in the web UI's **Settings**; engine settings are on the engine's card in **Models** › **Engines**."],[13601,"The **Add clips** part of a dataset's page offers several sources:"],[13240,"The **Export** tab:"],[13729,"the **Main clip** badge, or **Make it the main clip**. The main clip comes first when the voice is cloned, and is the one played from the list."],[14025,"The **Speak** button at the bottom is replaced by the one step the model still needs, here **Download Qwen3-TTS 1.7B CustomVoice (size)**. Click it and wait for the progress bar. (When torch is missing, it shows the command that installs it instead.)"],[13477,"The **Text** box takes up to 20,000 characters. Ctrl+Enter in it speaks."],[12109,"The `/dev` route (`DevComponentsView.vue`) shows every `ui/` component, for checking them by eye."],[11500,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository root builds one image: the server, its web UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends (and IndexTTS-2.5's Japanese with `GATED=1`). Models go into the `/data` volume."],[7348,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository's root builds one image with the Mizuoto server, its web UI and every engine, torch included; models download into the data volume."],[12052,"The `export` stage returns `{\"artifacts\": [...]}`, which the host's `_register` takes in:"],[9193,"The `MIZUOTO_` prefix is dropped and the rest lower-cased; `__` (two underscores) goes one level down: `MIZUOTO_COMPUTE__GPU_JOBS` is `compute.gpu_jobs`, `MIZUOTO_ENGINES__QWEN3TTS__DEVICE` is `engines.qwen3tts.device`, `MIZUOTO_REMOTE__AGENT__PORT` is `remote.agent.port`."],[9589,"The `mizuoto` command line does what the web UI does: speak, clone and design voices, convert and edit recordings, transcribe, check torch and the engines, manage models, presets, projects, datasets and training, remote hosts, jobs and settings. It is a thin wrapper: each command parses its arguments, calls the **one** core method for that operation and prints the result. The HTTP API behind the web UI calls the same methods, so both behave alike, and the records `--json` prints have the same shape as the API's JSON."],[11595,"The `ModelManager` (`manager.py`, ComfyUI's `load_models_gpu` / `free_memory`) keeps every registered handle with its owner (`<model id>@<device>`) and last use, and places handles **whole or partly** for each phase of a request (`ctx.use`, `ctx.run`): idle components give up memory unit by unit, a model that does not fit keeps part of its weights in RAM and streams them to the device as its layers run, and a phase that runs out of memory runs again, exactly, with more weights streamed. The policy (`policy.py`, `VramPolicy`) comes from the `compute` settings at each load."],[10205,"The `open_services()` context manager (the CLI's through `cli/output.py`), built once per command and closed after"],[9173,"The `paths.*` settings move models, voices, outputs, datasets, experiments, projects and caches elsewhere one by one; empty means inside the data folder."],[11506,"The `python:<version>-slim` base of the wheels stage and the image"],[12069,"The `ui/` wrapper layer"],[7308,"The `X-Mizuoto-Sample-Rate` header is the rate and `X-Mizuoto-Job` the job (the result is still stored). Streaming text is not available this way."],[12605,"The 1.5/2 front end: WeTextProcessing's FSTs through kaldifst (`TnProcessor`), `TextNormalizer`, SentencePiece, `split_segments`"],[12730,"The 12 Hz speech tokenizer: a Mimi-style encoder (transformers' `MimiModel` encode path) and a causal decoder (72-frame attention window, SnakeBeta upsampling)"],[12607,"The 2.5 front end: punctuation map, normalisation, fugashi for Japanese, tiktoken with `<\\|lang\\|>`"],[12439,"The 44.1 kHz codec"],[8101,"the above plus **Emotion from a clip**, **Emotion sliders**, **Emotion from text**, **Streaming**"],[7936,"the above plus **Preset speakers** (no inline tags)"],[9551,"The address this machine listens on as an agent; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[7688,"The address to bind"],[13311,"The address to listen on (`127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only) and the port (7869 by default). **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**"],[13956,"The address to listen on, `127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only"],[8514,"The advanced section is for readers who already use Mizuoto and want to know more about the engines, the API, remote hosts, performance, downloads, containers and calling it from Python."],[11686,"The agent answers each operation with `progress`, `chunk` (a binary frame: float32 little-endian mono) and `file` frames, then a `result` or `error`, and beats every 5 s. With no frame for `remote.heartbeat_timeout` (60 s), the host closes the session with `worker_failed` (`during = \"heartbeat\"`); the next request reconnects."],[8497,"The agent beats every 5 s while it works; a request whose agent stays silent this long fails"],[8464,"The agent cannot be reached"],[7408,"The agent has its own volume and models; build its image like the host's (same Mizuoto version, `GATED=1` if it serves the gated engines). The image's health check asks the web UI's port 7869, which an agent does not serve, hence `--no-healthcheck`. Without TLS, requests and audio cross the network unencrypted: use a trusted network, or give a certificate with `--ssl-certfile` / `--ssl-keyfile` (mount the files into the container)."],[8430,"The agent runs in the foreground until Ctrl+C. Its idle unloading and GPU memory handling follow that machine's settings (`compute.*`, `engines.<id>.*`). A port in use stops it with a hint to choose another `--port`."],[8441,"The agent serves TLS"],[8426,"The agent uses that machine's own data folder (settings, models, cache), as `mizuoto webui` there would; set `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` to give it another one. It runs the engines in its own process."],[8375,"The agent: the machine with the engines"],[9539,"The agent's `host:port` (port 7870 by default)"],[8437,"The agent's `host` or `host:port` (port 7870 by default); IPv6 as `[::1]:7870`"],[9554,"The agent's port"],[9560,"The agent's TLS certificate"],[9542,"The agent's token (`remote.agent.token` on that machine)"],[8439,"The agent's token. Left out when changing a host, the saved one is kept"],[9949,"The API (`mizuoto/api/`) and the command line (`mizuoto/cli/`) are two thin shells over one core: parse the input, call one core method, shape the output. This page covers both shells and their conventions; the core itself is in Architecture, and how the web UI consumes these endpoints is in Web UI."],[11748,"The API server (7869) and the Vite dev server (5173) together; Ctrl+C stops both"],[10539,"The app is built inside a function, not at import time, so each test gets a fresh one; `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py` compares the whole command tree, so a forgotten registration fails."],[9938,"The app: `create_app()`"],[10972,"the attempt's exception frame is left first (it holds the failed attempt's tensors);"],[11032,"The attention dispatcher"],[10650,"The attention policy is bound per request step for inference, and process-wide for a training stage"],[9747,"The attentions that add relative positions inside the scores, or need the probability matrix, are not sites: wenet's relative attention, IndexTTS's Conformer, w2v-BERT, VITS, plus the s3tokenizer (q and k each scaled by d^-¼), MelStyle and G2PW's BERT. They stay hand-written, since no fused kernel computes them. `Site(swappable=False)` keeps a site on its reference whatever the policy; `approx_ok=False` refuses every backend that is not exact."],[12644,"The audio is 8 codebooks of the HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer. The language model, Qwen3-0.6B run **bidirectionally**, sees the style tokens, the text, the reference's codes and the target as masked positions; over a fixed number of steps (32 by default) it unmasks the most confident codes, with classifier-free guidance in log-probability space, a per-codebook penalty and Gumbel noise on positions. Every step is a full forward over the whole sequence (no KV cache). The target length comes from a rule-based estimate (per-script character weights scaled by the reference's speaking rate), or from `speed` and `duration`."],[12234,"The audio is cut into 30 s windows overlapping by 5 s on each side, each window's features computed as `WhisperFeatureExtractor` computes them, four windows per `generate` call."],[9758,"the backends with a backward pass (not `sage`, `sage3`)"],[7239,"The body is a `SpeakRequest`. Its main fields (`/docs` has all of them):"],[7265,"The body of `PUT /api/v1/audio/files` is the file itself (not multipart); the `name` query parameter names it. The `id` it returns is a reference's `audio_id`:"],[10468,"The body says why, the measured or compared results, and any behaviour deliberately kept."],[10534,"The bound socket is handed to uvicorn (`server.run(sockets=[sock])`): there is no gap between checking and serving."],[12195,"The boundary that decides where code goes is now inside the package: **`mizuoto/core` never imports torch at module level**, and `mizuoto/core/inference` is its only door to model code (`mizuoto.runtime`, `mizuoto.nn`, `mizuoto.engines`, `mizuoto.training`), always imported inside functions. So `mizuoto version`, `mizuoto --help` and the core's own tests load no torch, and a command that never loads a model never imports the runtime. Architecture starts from that rule."],[10855,"The budget"],[10530,"The build uses `base: './'`, and at run time `api/baseUrl.ts` derives the deployment root from the entry script's URL (everything before the last `/assets/`); routes use hash history. One build works at the root and under an `--api-prefix` sub-path with no rewriting."],[11620,"The building blocks engines share live beside the runtime: `mizuoto/nn` (DSP bit-exact with torchaudio, librosa and Whisper; flows; transformers; vocoders; codecs; SSL and speaker encoders) and `mizuoto/text` (BPE tokenizers identical to transformers' for the models Mizuoto runs, Whisper's vocabulary, wetext's normaliser)."],[11725,"The built `dist/` ships in the wheel as package data; `mizuoto webui` from a checkout without `dist/` serves the API but no UI."],[9157,"the built-in defaults;"],[9839,"the call needs a backward pass or dropout it lacks;"],[11662,"The caller passes an `EngineRequest` with its `cancel` event (a job's `cancel_event`), an optional `timeout`, the streamed-text queue (`text_input`, filled by `TextFeed`) and a `progress` callback. A small watcher thread checks every 20 ms: it copies the caller's cancel into the context's cancel event, and past the timeout it marks the call timed out and cancels it. The engine stops at its next `check_cancel()`; the call then fails with `CancelledError`, or `OperationTimeoutError` after a timeout. When the call ends, the handle copies `applied`, `warnings` and `timings[\"total\"]` into the `EngineRequest`."],[13283,"The cast and each line's state (with chapter and line ids)"],[8942,"The cast and every line with its state"],[10610,"The catalogue downloads only files the engines read"],[8073,"The catalogue has no int8 version: no public repository exists for it."],[8425,"The certificate's private key"],[9073,"The certificate's private key"],[9135,"The certificate's private key"],[9563,"The certificate's private key"],[9231,"The certificate's private key, when the certificate file lacks it"],[8323,"the CFM estimator"],[9872,"the CFM estimator (each SoVITS model loaded, a voice's own too)"],[7293,"The client sends one JSON text message: a `SpeakRequest`."],[12660,"The closed design vocabulary and `_resolve_instruct`"],[10501,"The code as it is"],[11462,"The code has paths for these devices (device probing, float64 modules on the CPU where a device lacks float64, no compilation on MPS, CUDA graphs and half precision only on CUDA) and they are tested on simulated devices, but they have not been verified on AMD, Intel or Apple hardware."],[10026,"The code strings live in `mizuoto/core/codes.py` (standard library only), so engines and training stages raise them without pydantic; `error_from_code()` rebuilds the class from a code."],[9947,"The command line"],[13541,"The command line (`--span` is repeatable, `START:END[:SECONDS]` in seconds):"],[9649,"The command line and a server can open the same data folder at the same time. They are separate processes sharing the settings file, the database and the folders:"],[10202,"The command line and Python"],[13098,"The command line can name it, or move rather than copy: `mizuoto model import <folder> [--name name] [--move]`."],[10537,"The command line follows ani2xcur's Typer layout:"],[7344,"The command line in the container"],[13018,"The command line:"],[13023,"The command line:"],[13529,"The command line:"],[10475,"The command line: Typer registration"],[7395,"The command: `mizuoto webui --host 0.0.0.0 --port 7869 --no-open`."],[9573,"The commands"],[12068,"The component layer: `src/ui/`"],[12098,"The components `@material/web` has are wrapped in project Vue components: buttons (`AppButton`: filled, tonal, outlined, text), icon buttons, FAB, checkbox, filter chip, divider, text field and text area, slider, linear and circular progress, switch, tabs. The wrapper owns the props, the event names and the types; `vite.config.ts` declares `md-*` tags as custom elements."],[12850,"The conditions"],[8485,"The connection drops or the agent stops answering"],[11740,"The contract suite against the installed models (`MIZUOTO_TEST_DEVICE=cpu\\|cuda:N`)"],[12841,"The contract suite passes (18 tests across the three models)."],[12356,"The contract suite passes (18 tests)."],[10398,"The conventions code in Mizuoto follows: style, the layer rules, the rules for native code, the exactness rule, the steps for adding a command, route, setting or engine option, what tests a change needs, documentation in both languages and the commit message format."],[12437,"The conversation prompt, sampling in upstream's order, turn grouping, the decoder (`Decoder`) with its CUDA graphs"],[10716,"The core (`EngineRegistry`), without importing the engine"],[10444,"The core method (`Record` in and out) → a route with an `operation_id` in `api/routers/` → `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and commit `schema.d.ts` → `tests/api/test_api.py`. See Adding a route"],[10723,"The core plans and validates every request from the manifest alone, then calls the implementation through `core/inference` (see Runtime). This page walks through OmniVoice: `mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/omnivoice.toml` and `mizuoto/engines/omnivoice/`."],[12187,"The core, the API, the command line, the web UI (its built `dist/` ships in the wheel), the runtime, the building blocks and every engine under a permissive licence"],[10458,"The core's behaviour is tested with the dummy engine (no torch, no model); the network is replaced by `httpx.MockTransport`; tests get an isolated data folder and an empty environment from `make_services`."],[10576,"The cost of running in process (a crash in native code takes the server down; no memory release by process exit) is paid for by rules"],[12353,"the CosyVoice 3 English clone: about 23 dB (CAM++'s float noise, above);"],[12259,"The CosyVoice engine as implemented in Mizuoto: CosyVoice 1, 2 and 3, speech tokenizers and CAM++ from their ONNX files, the language models, flows and HiFT, what reproduces upstream exactly and why the whole stack is not bit-identical, the GPU decoding path, the LLM and flow fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[7683,"the data folder"],[9127,"the data folder"],[7386,"The data folder"],[7679,"The data folder"],[9183,"The data folder"],[7608,"The data folder (database, models, voices, outputs, caches)"],[10091,"The data folder and compatibility"],[9141,"The data folder and the settings file"],[10263,"The data folder defaults to `mizuoto` in the platform's user data folder (`~/.local/share/mizuoto` on Linux, under `%APPDATA%` on Windows, under `~/Library/Application Support` on macOS); `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` puts it elsewhere. It holds `models/` (with `_assets/`), `voices/`, `outputs/`, `datasets/`, `experiments/`, `projects/`, `cache/` (with `scratch/<engine>/`, the requests' scratch folders), `uploads/`, `logs/`, `jobs/` (job logs), `server.json` (the running server's address and process id) and `mizuoto.db`. Most folders can be moved with `paths.*`."],[9162,"The data folder holds the settings, the database, models, voices and outputs. By default:"],[13958,"The data folder to use this time"],[7528,"the data folder's models folder"],[7753,"The data on this page comes from each engine's manifest (`mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/<id>.toml`). To see what applies on your machine, use the command line:"],[7630,"The database"],[13979,"The database: jobs, results, cached transcripts and more"],[12016,"The dataset's fingerprint is the SHA-256 of its `manifest.jsonl`; `hp` is the method's defaults merged with the experiment's values. When states are read (`_with_status`), a finished stage whose fingerprint differs from the current one is `stale`, and so is every finished stage after it. Changing the learning rate therefore makes only the training stage that reads it, and what follows, stale; feature extraction before it stays done."],[10571,"The decisions that shaped the code as it is: what was decided, and why."],[11216,"The decoding loop at the 1.7B model's sizes, random weights, 4 or 8 of its 28 talker layers, 100 frames, batch 1 (the 1.7B model did not fit beside the other workload); ms per frame, best warm run of two interleaved rounds:"],[11265,"The decoding loop with the real fast transformer, 2 or 4 of its 36 slow layers, random weights, 60 frames (S2 Pro, 11 GB, did not fit); ms per frame, torch 2.8:"],[8135,"The default data folder:"],[8134,"The default port is 7869. When it is taken, the server tries the next ports (20 at most) and logs \"Port 7869 is unavailable. Using port 7870.\"; the browser opens the port actually used, and stdout gets a line `SERVER_READY url=…` once it listens."],[10281,"The default; dataset preparation; a training run on the CPU"],[13093,"The delete button deletes the model's files (asking **Delete** *model*? **It can be downloaded again.**)."],[11707,"The development tools are also listed in `[dependency-groups] dev` of `pyproject.toml`. Without the two gated packages their tests skip and their engines show as missing."],[9849,"the device and compute capability;"],[8224,"the device for engines set to `auto`; `auto` picks the GPU with the most free memory, else the CPU. UI: **Settings** › **Compute** › **Default device**"],[8476,"The device names no known host"],[9499,"The device training uses (the first); empty: the engine's own device. A fine-tune takes the device for itself while it runs"],[13320,"The device used by engines whose device is automatic; any device found on this machine"],[10955,"The device's `Streamer`:"],[8227,"the devices Mizuoto may use, such as `[\"cuda:0\"]`; empty: all"],[13021,"The dialog shows the licence's full text and a link to the original. Read it, then check **I have read and accept this licence**."],[10829,"The diffusion language model on `mizuoto.runtime.lm.qwen`'s decoder"],[10568,"The diffusion machinery (samplers, hooks, ControlNet), and running language models as text encoders."],[8319,"the DiT (or E2's UNetT)"],[9868,"the DiT, or E2's UNetT"],[11387,"The docs site"],[11894,"The docs site (`site/`) has its own vitest tests; `src/lib/i18n-content.test.ts` requires a `<slug>.en.mdx` for every Chinese `<slug>.mdx` and the same page order in both sidebars."],[11759,"The docs site has its own tasks: `site-install`, `site-dev`, `site` and `test-site` (see Release). The parity harness is not a `dev.py` task; it lives in `scripts/parity/` (see Testing)."],[10085,"The door to model code: `core/inference`"],[12435,"The dual-AR transformer"],[11771,"The dummy engine"],[14017,"The dummy engine ships with Mizuoto: nothing to download, and it needs no torch. It speaks in tones instead of words, but goes through exactly the same steps as a real engine."],[13089,"The dummy engine's model; nothing to download"],[9093,"The effective settings (the access token only as set or not)"],[9156,"The effective settings are four layers, each overriding the ones before it:"],[12603,"The emotion model: Qwen3-0.6B, greedy, its chat template, the answer parsed into eight weights"],[8610,"The emotion, described"],[13160,"The end of a paragraph (the pause after a paragraph is longer when exported)"],[9385,"The endpoint for `custom`: a Hugging Face compatible server"],[12229,"The engine answers one operation, `call(\"transcribe\", {\"path\", \"language\", \"options\"})`, which returns `{text, language, segments, duration}`. `AsrService` holds one lock for it and caches transcripts by the audio's SHA-256 and the model."],[7636,"The engine catalogue and states: `status(id)` says whether an engine is available"],[11791,"The engine contract suite against installed models (`dev.py test-engines`)"],[11576,"The engine contract; `BUILTIN` and the `mizuoto.engines` entry points"],[10763,"The engine id (the manifest's and the registry's)"],[10728,"The engine id; the implementation is registered under the same id"],[7856,"The engine is a distribution of its own (`mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`); downloading models and shared files, and synthesis, need the licence accepted first: **Accept the licence** in **Models** › **Engines**, or `mizuoto engine accept-licence <id>`. `mizuoto engine licence <id>` prints the full text"],[13445,"The engine is disabled under **Models › Engines**"],[8482,"The engine is not available on the agent (torch or its package is missing)"],[13449,"The engine is not available: torch, or a licence-gated engine's package, is not installed. Install it into Mizuoto's Python, then restart Mizuoto"],[10086,"The engine registry and manifests"],[8792,"The engine the weights are for, e.g. `gptsovits` (required)"],[7152,"The engine's licence is not accepted yet"],[12847,"The engines"],[8390,"The engines, in the agent's own process; loaded models, idle unloading"],[8889,"The engines, whether each is available, its licence, whether it is enabled, its model count"],[10575,"The engines' dependency conflicts (transformers 4.51 to 5.3, torch 2.3 and 2.8, numpy 1 and 2) all came from upstream code using library internals and from upstream pins, not from what the models need. Ported, they need one torch and one set of dependencies, and the engine environments, worker processes and inter-process protocol go"],[12172,"The entry point for contributors: what Mizuoto is made of, what is authoritative, and what each development page covers."],[11692,"The environment and tasks needed to go from a fresh clone to the dev server, every check and a real engine."],[9105,"The environment variables Mizuoto reads, and the `MIZUOTO_*` variables set now (values of names containing `TOKEN` show as `***`). Option: `--json`."],[10688,"The error codes `download_failed` (exit 12) and `install_failed` (13)"],[10639,"The estimate comes from file sizes and is not calibrated on a GPU"],[7628,"The event bus: `subscribe(handler)`"],[10049,"The events today: `settings_changed`, `job_updated`, `job_log`, `jobs_cleared`, `outputs_added`, `outputs_removed`, `runtime_changed`, `compute_changed`, `engines_changed`, `voices_changed`, `datasets_changed`, `projects_changed`, `experiments_changed`, `train_metrics`, `presets_changed`, `models_changed`. Each carries a snapshot, never a live object: the bridge serialises it later on the event loop while job threads keep writing. The bridge subscribes to the EventBus (called from threads, it crosses into the loop with `call_soon_threadsafe`) and emits each event under its name."],[13664,"The experiment's page shows the base model, the dataset, the result and the language. **Stages** is a row of steps, each **Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date** or **Failed**."],[9519,"The export stage speaks a dataset clip's text with what was trained"],[12361,"The F5-TTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v1 Base, v0 Base and E2, the DiT and UNetT, the CFM sampler and Vocos, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and compile notes, the full fine-tune, and its parity results."],[12359,"The fast decoding path is CUDA only."],[8339,"the fastest backend this device offers: on NVIDIA GPUs with fp16/bf16 models SageAttention, FlashAttention, xFormers when installed, else PyTorch's SDPA; elsewhere SDPA"],[10260,"The file is checked for outside changes every second; every change, wherever it came from, reaches the `on_keys_change` listeners as dotted keys (`changed_keys`)."],[11896,"The first job, `scope`, reads the changed files (a push's from the compare API, a pull request's from its file list) and `python scripts/ci.py scope` maps them to checks:"],[13950,"The first port to try, from the settings by default (7869); `0` picks any free port"],[11368,"The first request pays the compilation: +30 s to +160 s. The audio is not identical (Acceleration)."],[8329,"The first requests pay the compilation: on a CPU, 30 s to 160 s more."],[12992,"The first synthesis"],[13029,"The first synthesis loads the model into the server's process, which takes a while; then the model stays in memory until it has been idle for the time set under **Settings › Compute**. When the GPU has less free memory than the model needs, Mizuoto fails at once with **The GPU is not available or ran out of memory**, and **What to do** says how to fix it, such as another device or freeing GPU memory."],[13440,"The first time, the screen picks **Settings › Speech › Default model**, or else the first model that is ready. Then it remembers your last choice."],[12417,"The Fish Speech S2 Pro engine as implemented in Mizuoto's separate mizuoto-fishspeech distribution: the dual-AR transformer and the 44.1 kHz codec, what reproduces upstream exactly, one wait per frame and CUDA graphs, the LoRA fine-tune, and its parity results."],[8321,"the flow estimator"],[9870,"the flow estimator"],[7682,"The folder for `settings.toml` (your application's configuration folder, for instance); the data stays in `data_dir`"],[9185,"The folder for `settings.toml`, when it should not sit in the data folder"],[7611,"The folder holding `settings.toml`"],[10673,"The folders are the truth, and a scan cannot drift from the files; hundreds of voices scan in milliseconds"],[12097,"The font (`@fontsource-variable/roboto-flex`) and the icons are bundled into `dist/`: the UI loads nothing from outside and works offline."],[10623,"The former need another model and a ModelScope pipeline, and are all off in upstream's default generation; there is no public int8 repository"],[12525,"The front end: `frontend.py` (cleaner, `TextPreprocessor`), segmentation, language detection (split-lang, fast-langdetect), Chinese (tone sandhi, normalisation, G2PW), English (normalisation, tagger, g2p_en), Japanese, Korean (g2pk2), Cantonese, symbols and data"],[11533,"The frontmatter has `title`, `description` and `icon` (a Lucide icon name). The MDX components are in `site/src/components/mdx.tsx`: `Cards`/`Card`, `Callout`, `Tabs`/`Tab`, `Steps`/`Step`, `Accordions`/`Accordion` and `Mermaid` (a `chart` prop; rendered in the browser with Mermaid loaded from a CDN, following the site's light or dark theme)."],[13912,"The full development setup is in Development setup."],[10740,"The full list is `Capability` in `models.py`. Some drive the pipeline: without `long_text` Mizuoto segments the text; `batch` with `max_batch > 1` enables micro-batching; `stream_audio`'s granularity comes from `stream_granularity`; `stream_text_input` allows streamed text over the WebSocket. A variant may also have `languages`, `speakers`, `emotions`, `inline_tags`, `instruct_requires` and `weights_version`."],[12793,"The generation comes from `config.json`'s `architecture` (missing means `voxcpm`); 1.5 is the first generation with a 44.1 kHz VAE. The model folder holds `config.json`, `model.safetensors` (else `pytorch_model.bin`), `audiovae.pth` (else `audiovae.safetensors`), `tokenizer.json` and `tokenizer_config.json`. A voice's cache holds the VAE latents of the prompt (left-padded) and of the reference (right-padded), as upstream's `build_prompt_cache` makes them."],[11206,"The generator jumped ahead instead of drawing: MT19937's state after *n* draws computed in GF(2) (`mizuoto/training/rng.py`), 204 jumps in 2.3 s instead of 41–52 s"],[12544,"The GPT is small and launch-bound: a step is about 360 small kernels and used to wait for the device twice (upstream's two end-of-sequence checks), plus a Python boolean copied to the device by top-p. Now the two checks are read together (the same boolean) and the copy is a `fill_`: one wait per step. With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device) its one-token steps run as graphs around each layer's attention, one set per number of rows (rows drop as they finish); the cache, grown by concatenation, and the sampling stay eager on the request's generator. A voice's own GPT gets its own graphs. The real v2, v2Pro and v4 models give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.3–2.0 times faster per request."],[9913,"the GPT-2's one-token steps around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling eager"],[12466,"The GPT-SoVITS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v2, v2Pro, v2ProPlus, v4 and v5 Turbo, the text front end with its ported converters and models, the T2S model, SoVITS and the flow, what reproduces upstream exactly, GPU decoding, the speaker fine-tune that writes upstream's files, and its parity results."],[8452,"The handshake succeeded"],[10831,"The HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer: `nn/codecs/dac`, `nn/ssl/hubert`, residual codebooks"],[13031,"The History screen: every result, to search, filter by model, mark as favourite, run again, download and delete."],[11684,"The host connects and sends `hello` with the token (compared with `hmac.compare_digest`) and its protocol. An agent of another protocol refuses the host with a hint to install the same Mizuoto version on both machines, and the host refuses such an agent in turn. Otherwise the agent answers with its `AgentInfo`: version, devices, which engines are available there and its installed models."],[7738,"The host enters the child app's `lifespan` on its own event loop (it forwards events to the socket) and calls `services.close()` on the way out. `start_background=True` starts the job scheduler and the unloading of idle models; without it, queued jobs do not run. `create_app` also takes `extra_hosts` (a set; names added to it later are accepted at once) and `serve_ui=False` (the API only)."],[8446,"The host is contacted at once: online, the command prints the agent's machine name, Mizuoto version, devices and installed engines; unreachable, the host is saved anyway and its state (`offline` or `refused`) is shown."],[11688,"The host plans against its own catalogue and the agent's model list; the agent handles its own GPU memory, and training always stays local."],[10644,"The host probes devices without importing torch: nvidia-smi, rocm-smi / amd-smi and the platform first, a child process only when torch's build could see a GPU the tools missed"],[8376,"The host: the machine that uses remote engines"],[7550,"The Hugging Face repository"],[12314,"The HyperPyYAML file read as data (`!new:`/`!name:` as dicts, `!ref` expressions resolved)"],[11522,"the image"],[13930,"The image has a health check (`/api/v1/app/health`)."],[7404,"The image's environment variables apply to `docker exec` too, so commands work on the same data folder:"],[13928,"The image's Python"],[10717,"The implementation: an `Engine` subclass and its `LoadedEngine`, built on `mizuoto.runtime`, `mizuoto.nn` and `mizuoto.text`"],[10765,"The implementation's own version string (default `\"1\"`). Voice caches are keyed by Mizuoto's version, not this one"],[10240,"The implementations' registry is in `runtime/engine.py`: built-in engines are listed in `BUILTIN` (`id → module:Class`), other distributions register through the entry-point group `mizuoto.engines`. Entry points are read once per process, so installing an engine package means restarting Mizuoto."],[12556,"The IndexTTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto's separate mizuoto-indextts distribution: IndexTTS-1.5, 2 and 2.5, the GPT-2 with beam sampling, conditioning, emotion and the s2mel decoder, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and GPU decoding, and its parity results."],[11059,"The inference set is thirteen cases: Qwen3-TTS `base-clone-en` and `cv-en-aiden`, F5-TTS `clone-en`, OmniVoice `clone-en`, CosyVoice `v2-clone-en` and `v3-clone-en`, GPT-SoVITS `v2-clone-zh` and `v4-clone-zh`, Fish Speech `clone-en`, IndexTTS `v2-clone-en` and `v15-clone-en`, VoxCPM `v2-clone-en` and `v15-clone-en`. The training set is one fine-tune per trainer on an 11-clip dataset."],[7315,"The installed speech models (not speech recognition), and the aliases in `tts.model_aliases`"],[12219,"The internal speech recognition engine: Whisper large-v3-turbo implemented in Mizuoto, reproducing the transformers pipeline Mizuoto 0.1 used, with its 5-beam search, overlapping windows, seek loop and merge; its memory notes and parity results."],[13647,"the issues: **too short**, **too long**, **without text**, **clipping**, each with **Show them** to list only those clips;"],[12150,"The jobs this session knows: every active job, and those that finished while the page was open; the screen each was started from (`upsert(job, from)`, `fromScreen()`); `onFinished