e API is how other programs (and `mizuoto runtime`) see and free them. `routers/runtime.py`:"],[8821,"The models Mizuoto knows, and their states"],[13004,"The models of Fish Speech and IndexTTS cannot be downloaded until their licences are accepted. See Licence-gated engines below."],[13063,"The Models screen: download, verify, delete and import catalogue models; engine cards (availability, device, precision, enabled, options, checks, licence); and shared files."],[13994,"The models, voices, results and cache folders can be moved under **Settings › Storage** (for example `models/` to a larger disk)."],[7556,"The ModelScope repository"],[9437,"The most characters in one request (at least 100)"],[13162,"the name is already in the cast;"],[10166,"The native runtime (built lazily), which engines are implemented here, their extras and trainers"],[11443,"The native trainers"],[13754,"The navigation is on the left (at the bottom in a narrow window):"],[12650,"The network: the bidirectional Qwen3 over text and audio codes (`audio_embeddings`, `audio_heads`)"],[13194,"The new line keeps this line's speaker"],[7729,"The object is also a context manager:"],[7432,"The official repositories"],[12631,"The OmniVoice engine as implemented in Mizuoto: the bidirectional Qwen3 with iterative unmasking, the HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer (DAC and HuBERT), pydub's arithmetic without pydub, what reproduces upstream exactly, the full and LoRA fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[9904,"the one-token steps (`DecoderSteps`) and the draw, a graph per EOS mask; upstream's nucleus loop replayed on the device (`nucleus_device`)"],[7052,"The OpenAPI schema also lists the socket's event types, so a client's types can be generated from it."],[10686,"The OpenAPI schema is generated without `separate_input_output_schemas=False`"],[11017,"the optimizer's sums may differ in the last bits on a GPU"],[10590,"The optional attention packages (flash-attn, xFormers, SageAttention) are backends only, with version checks, self-tests and fallbacks, never dependencies"],[12754,"The order comes from a plain shuffled data loader on the process-wide generator (the training stage's own process). Accelerate's gradient accumulation is reproduced as the loss over the steps, an optimiser step every N batches and at each epoch's end."],[12137,"The other `*_changed` events invalidate their keys through `createInvalidator()`, so a burst within 300 ms causes one refetch."],[13746,"The other commands (`add-ref`, `set-transcript`, `retranscribe`, `edit`, `remove`…) are in `mizuoto voice --help` and the command reference. `voice add`, `voice from-output` and `voice edit` take `--consent`, an optional note on whose voice it is that is stored with the voice (`voice info` prints it); nothing requires it."],[12257,"The out-of-memory fallback can change a transcript in rare ties."],[9527,"The output file name: `{date}` (`YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS`), `{voice}`, `{model}` (the model's name without the engine), `{engine}`; unknown fields are empty, and a clash adds `-1`, `-2`…"],[7507,"The output folder"],[7523,"The output folder"],[11484,"The output goes to `dist/` by default. The script uses the standard library plus uv and bun."],[11485,"The package data that ships in the wheel is listed in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.setuptools.package-data]`): the built UI, the engine manifests, files manifests and licence texts, F5-TTS's vocabulary, GPT-SoVITS's text front-end data, Whisper's vocabulary. IndexTTS's text-normalisation FSTs ship in `mizuoto-indextts`."],[11923,"The package on the oldest Mizuoto its `pyproject.toml` allows (`python scripts/ci.py lower-bound <id>`), from PyPI: its tests run outside the checkout, with only `tests/` on `PYTHONPATH`, so `import mizuoto` finds the released one (the range check, which compares the range with Mizuoto at this commit, is left out)"],[8351,"The packages are not dependencies. Each is tied to a torch version, a CUDA or ROCm runtime and a GPU generation, so you install them yourself, without letting them replace your torch. `mizuoto doctor` lists which are installed and whether each runs on each GPU (a tiny self-test), and gives the command for this machine. For example: `pip install \"xformers==0.0.32.post2\" --no-deps` for torch 2.8.0, `pip install flash-attn --no-build-isolation --no-deps` (it compiles), `pip install sageattention==2.2.0 --no-build-isolation --no-deps` (it needs `nvcc`)."],[13695,"The page footer"],[13751,"The page footer"],[12154,"The page's one player (`audio/player.ts`)"],[11637,"The parameter values the engine actually used, and its warnings: both come back with the result"],[12037,"The parsed request; `rows` are `Row`s (`id`, `audio`, `text`, `speaker`, `language`, `duration`, `sample_rate`); dataset clips are FLAC (`mizuoto.nn.dsp.flac.read_audio` reads them)"],[13292,"The parts of Settings: General, Compute, Remote hosts, Speech, Training, Downloads, Storage, Appearance and About."],[7622,"The path arguments are `pathlib.Path`s. Without `with`, call `build_services()` yourself and `services.close()` when done."],[10084,"The path of a request"],[10975,"the phase runs again: the same draws, the same result, slower. At most two retries; the output records `applied.oom_retries` and a warning."],[9827,"The pinned SDPA kernels are called through their aten operators and ask torch's own eligibility test (`can_use_*_attention`) before they take a call. The optional packages' kernels are called directly: flash-attn and xFormers register their own operators and autograd; SageAttention has no backward and is never used under autograd."],[12710,"The preset speakers without instructions (upstream drops them silently for the 0.6B, so the variant does not declare them)"],[12414,"The pretrained weights are CC-BY-NC-4.0 and so is a fine-tune of them; outputs are tagged."],[7859,"The pretrained weights are CC-BY-NC-4.0; nothing to accept, but results are tagged and carry a notice"],[11677,"The process"],[10734,"The project and commit the port reproduces (documentation, not a dependency)"],[12161,"The Projects screen (long-form scripts read line by line by a cast of voices) is the most recent complete screen and makes a good template. Its API is `mizuoto/api/routers/projects.py`; its event is `projects_changed`."],[13123,"The Projects screen: a cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line; importing scripts, editing lines, rendering, takes and exporting audio with subtitles."],[12720,"The prompt as `Qwen3TTSForConditionalGeneration.generate` builds it, the talker loop, chunked decoding, voice caches"],[12429,"The prompt is a ChatML conversation: a system turn holding each reference's text and its codes, then the text to speak. The **slow transformer** (Qwen3-4B-shaped: 36 layers, q/k RMSNorm, one fused `wqkv`) generates a frame's semantic token; the **fast transformer** (4 layers) generates the other nine codebooks from the slow model's normed hidden state. The **codec** (a modified DAC at 44.1 kHz: causal convolutions, a windowed transformer, a downsampling residual quantiser with one semantic codebook of 4096 and nine of 1024; about 21.5 frames a second) encodes references and decodes frames into audio. Text is generated in batches of speaker turns, each batch decoded as it finishes."],[10252,"The protocol version is `AGENT_PROTOCOL = 2`. At `hello` the token is compared with `hmac.compare_digest` and the protocol checked; a host and an agent of different protocols refuse each other with an upgrade hint."],[11693,"The Python environment"],[7375,"The Python of the image (`python:<version>-slim`)"],[12949,"The Qwen2/Qwen3 decoder with transformers' numerics (`hf_sdpa`, `mask_for`), `DynamicCache` and the optional preallocated `BufferCache`"],[12688,"The Qwen3-TTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: variants and files, the talker, code predictor, speaker encoder and 12 Hz codec, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and CUDA-graph decoding, the speaker fine-tune, and its parity results."],[11279,"The real CosyVoice 2 LM (2 GB, it fit), 150 tokens, ms per token:"],[11334,"The real models did not fit wholly beside the other workload, so through the stack their weights streamed and graphs did not engage: the removed waits alone gave v1.5 10.25 → 9.59 s and v2 36.3 → 33.4 s (×1.07–1.09), identical audio. The decoding loop at the 1.5 GPT's sizes, 4 or 8 of its 24 layers, random weights, fp16, three beams, 120 steps; ms per step:"],[8663,"The recording to convert"],[8680,"The recording to edit"],[8684,"The recording's whole text after the edit (required)"],[12849,"The reference"],[9846,"The reference ignores it and uses the dense mask, so `auto` is unchanged. Qwen's `mask_for` returns `Masked(dense, info)`; VoxCPM's steps, Seed-VC, GPT-SoVITS v4/v5 and Fish Speech's codec give theirs. With `dispatch.DEBUG` on (the tiny engines' tests), every call checks that `mask_info` describes its dense mask; `MIZUOTO_TEST_ACCEL=count` checks that every site of every tiny engine and trainer goes through the dispatcher."],[12351,"The reference is upstream on torch 2.8 (on its own torch 2.3.1 it disagrees with itself on 2.8). With upstream's voice prompt fed to both, cloning (English, Chinese with numbers), cross-lingual cloning, instructions, preset speakers, streamed audio and voice conversion are identical sample for sample for v1, v2 and v3. Through the stack, each side making its own prompt:"],[11831,"The reference to clone comes from `MIZUOTO_TEST_REFERENCE` (plus `MIZUOTO_TEST_REFERENCE_TEXT`), else an installed preset or design model speaks one. Licence-gated engines take part only with `MIZUOTO_TEST_ACCEPT_LICENCES=1` (and their packages installed), and their licences are accepted in the temporary folder only."],[10274,"The registered kinds are `speak`, `voice_prepare`, `convert`, `edit`, `engine_op`, `transcribe`, `model_download`, `asset_download`, `dataset_prepare`, `train`, `project_render` and `project_export`."],[9852,"The registry, policies, fallbacks, strict mode and binding are tested on the CPU, with real models through every site (identical audio, metrics and weights with `auto`) and the optional backends' glue against fake packages computing the same maths. The optional kernels themselves, their speed and their quality are not measured yet."],[9078,"The remote hosts: address, state, version, devices, engines, the engines using it"],[13549,"The report"],[7563,"The repository to check"],[11543,"The request context"],[11631,"The request's `random.Random`, seeded the same way"],[11629,"The request's `torch.Generator` on a device, one per device, seeded with the request's seed (fresh entropy without one)"],[10974,"the request's generators, its `rng` and any the engine names (`generators=`) are put back as they were before the first attempt;"],[10799,"The requests and results are standard-library dataclasses in `mizuoto/core/inference/tasks.py`, re-exported by `mizuoto.runtime.engine`:"],[13829,"The REST API, a WebSocket for events and streamed audio, an OpenAI-compatible `/v1/audio/speech`, and Python."],[11860,"The result: on the CPU in fp32, every engine is identical to its reference (VoxCPM in bf16 too), except CosyVoice when each side makes its own voice prompt: CAM++'s speaker embedding differs from onnxruntime's by about 1e-6, and HiFT's sine source accumulates and amplifies that along the utterance; given the same voice prompt, CosyVoice is identical sample for sample too. Every trainer gives upstream's losses, learning rates and weights byte for byte on the CPU when both are seeded alike."],[10583,"The right build depends on the hardware and driver, which no package manager can choose for the user"],[12656,"The rule-based duration estimate, upstream's tables"],[10659,"The run holds the device once; the UI and the fingerprints know the stages without running anything"],[8487,"The running request fails; the next one reconnects"],[8360,"The running request takes the queued requests of its 