rong variant, the engine runs on a remote host, the model is not installed, the engine is not available, it has no trainer, the device kind does not fit, the trainer's `REQUIRES` do not import, training assets are missing. Each reason carries the command that fixes it."],[12355,"the training cross-load cases (one implementation's export spoken by the other): 57.4 and 38.1 dB."],[10640,"The training memory tools offer what keeps results and a few things that change them slightly; no Adafactor, no splitting micro-batches on out-of-memory"],[12194,"The two licence-gated engines are separate distributions only because of their licences. They install into the same environment and register themselves under the Python entry-point group `mizuoto.engines`."],[10531,"The UI is built before the wheel: `scripts/build_wheels.py` runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and `bun run build`, then builds the sdist and the wheel; Docker builds it in a bun stage of its own, and the final image carries no Node toolchain. See Release."],[12080,"The UI is built on Material Design 3 (M3) in two layers: a **token layer** that everything reads, and a **component layer** on top of it. The token layer depends on no component library; the component layer can be replaced piece by piece."],[14013,"The UI opens on **Speak**; nothing has to be set up before you try it. Two settings are worth a look before downloading a real model:"],[12994,"The UI opens on **Speak**. Nothing has to be set up first: the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones), so you can look around before downloading anything. Three places matter for a real engine:"],[13773,"The UI opens on the screen you were last on. Each screen keeps its state (and scroll position) while you visit others; the page of each voice, dataset, experiment and project keeps its own."],[10543,"The UI uses Material Design 3 in two layers:"],[13307,"The UI's language; **Auto** follows the browser"],[10869,"The user-facing settings are in Performance; the runtime as a whole in Runtime."],[10071,"The usual shape of a command (`commands/projects.py`):"],[12523,"The v4/v5 48 kHz HiFi-GAN; the ERes2NetV2 speaker-verification embedding"],[10989,"the VAE in tiles"],[7731,"The values in `settings` sit above the settings file and the environment, are **never written to the file**, and cannot be changed through the web UI or the API:"],[12714,"The variant comes from `config.json` (`tts_model_type`, `tts_model_size`); only `tokenizer_type = qwen3_tts_tokenizer_12hz` is accepted. The model folder holds `config.json`, `model.safetensors`, the tokenizer files (`tokenizer.json`, or `vocab.json` + `merges.txt` + `tokenizer_config.json`) and `speech_tokenizer/` (`config.json`, `model.safetensors`). A Base voice's cache is `prompt.pt`, the clone prompt (reference codes and speaker embedding)."],[12500,"The variant comes from the base GPT and SoVITS pair in the model folder, laid out as upstream lays it out: `gsv-v2final-pretrained/…`, `s1v3.ckpt`, `v2Pro/s2Gv2Pro.pth` / `s2Gv2ProPlus.pth`, `gsv-v4-pretrained/{s2Gv4,vocoder}.pth`, `gsv-v5-pretrained/{s2Gv5turbo,vocoder}.pth`. A voice's own weights (`Voice.weights[\"gptsovits\"]`: a GPT `.ckpt` and a SoVITS `.pth`, version read from the file) replace the base pair for that voice."],[12306,"The variant comes from the yaml in the folder (`cosyvoice.yaml`, `cosyvoice2.yaml`, `cosyvoice3.yaml`); a CosyVoice 1 folder with `spk2info.pt` is SFT or Instruct. The folder holds the yaml, `llm.pt`, `flow.pt`, `hift.pt`, `campplus.onnx`, `speech_tokenizer_v1.onnx` / `v2` / `v3`, `spk2info.pt`, and for v2/v3 the `CosyVoice-BlankEN` config and tokenizer (not its weights, which `llm.pt` replaces). The shared asset `cosyvoice/wetext` holds the text normaliser's FSTs. The ONNX models are converted once and cached as `<model>/.mizuoto/converted-<key>.safetensors` (a `<name>.safetensors` beside the ONNX file wins)."],[10773,"The variant from the folder's files only, without torch"],[9848,"the version: flash-attn ≥ 2.6; xFormers outside 0.0.21–0.0.26 (broken for large batches) and with its C++ kernels (`_has_cpp_library`: a wheel for another torch imports without them);"],[9104,"The versions of Mizuoto, Python and the main components (torch, fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, typer, httpx, numpy, av, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`; a component that is not installed has no version). Option: `--json`."],[7080,"The voice library"],[9244,"The voice library"],[10190,"The voice library (folders), fit, design, export/import"],[13983,"The voice library, one folder per voice"],[8389,"The voice library, reference clips and voice caches"],[7656,"The voice library: `list_voices`, `get`, `create_from_audio`"],[13686,"The voice library: make voices from audio, design them, add preset speakers, manage clips, transcripts and fine-tuned weights, see which models can use them, export and import."],[13764,"The voice library: make, design, import and export voices, and see which models can use them"],[13808,"The voice library: voices from clips (speech recognition fills in missing transcripts), designed voices, preset speakers and voices with their own fine-tuned weights; export and import."],[12308,"The voice prompt is made from the reference three times over: 16 kHz audio to a Whisper log-mel to the **speech tokenizer**'s tokens; 16 kHz audio to a kaldi fbank to **CAM++**'s 192-dim speaker embedding; and always a 24 kHz Matcha mel, even for the 22.05 kHz CosyVoice 1. The **language model** turns text (and the prompt's text and tokens) into speech tokens; the **flow** turns tokens into a mel in 10 Euler steps with guidance 0.7; **HiFT** (a HiFi-GAN with a neural source filter and an inverse STFT) turns the mel into audio."],[8646,"The voice, described"],[8744,"The voice, described"],[13225,"The voice: **Library voice**, **Preset speaker** or **Its own voice**, as the model supports. The library picker shows how this model can use each voice, as in Speak."],[13569,"the voice's GPT and SoVITS weights"],[8725,"The voice's language"],[8719,"The voice's name"],[8740,"The voice's name"],[13689,"The voice's page"],[12763,"The VoxCPM engine as implemented in Mizuoto: VoxCPM2, 1.5 and 0.5B, MiniCPM-4, the local DiT and the AudioVAE, the tokenizer and normaliser as upstream's locked libraries build them, what reproduces upstream exactly, patch decoding with CUDA graphs, the full and LoRA fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[9914,"The waits were removed with exact equivalents of upstream's idioms (masked assignments, list indices, Python scalars stored into tensors, `.item()` checks), and the stop flag is read once per step. `dispatch.DEBUG`'s mask check is skipped while a stream captures (it reads back; the warm-up checked)."],[11062,"The warm request before the CPU rounds:"],[11049,"The warm runs of two rounds side by side, the speed-up and the phases that changed most"],[12232,"The WAV is read as soundfile reads it (channels averaged) and resampled to 16 kHz by soxr (its HQ default)."],[9003,"The ways a model can be fine-tuned, with their stages and hyperparameters"],[11724,"The web UI (`mizuoto/webui/`) and the docs site (`site/`) use bun to install, build and test. `dev.py` looks for `bun` on `PATH`, then in the installer's default `~/.bun/bin`, and gives a clear error, not a traceback, when neither has it."],[12078,"The web UI is a Vue 3 project in `mizuoto/webui/`. Its components are Material Web (`@material/web`), its icons Lucide (`@lucide/vue`), its data layer TanStack Query (`@tanstack/vue-query`) with `openapi-fetch`, its state Pinia. The build, `mizuoto/webui/dist/`, ships in the wheel as package data and is served by the API's `SPAStaticFiles` (see HTTP API and command line). The base (`theme/`, `ui/`, motion, layers, the shell, stores, i18n, rule tests) is rvc-next's; where it comes from is in Design references and decisions."],[8156,"The web UI opens on **Speak**, where the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones); there is no setup screen. Choose the download source under **Settings** › **Downloads**, check torch under **Settings** › **Compute** (or with `mizuoto doctor`), then download models from **Models**, or with the button that replaces **Speak** when the chosen model is not downloaded, and follow them in **Jobs**. See First run."],[7354,"The web UI, built with bun (`mizuoto/webui/dist`)"],[8393,"The web UI, the HTTP API, the command line"],[11699,"The web UI: bun"],[7726,"The web UI's address, the port, whether it serves"],[13748,"The web UI's layout: navigation, the jobs sheet, the models in memory, the theme, and the guide to each screen."],[11427,"The weights in ONNX files are converted into torch modules by an in-tree protobuf reader (`runtime/convert/onnx.py`), the result cached under the model folder's `.mizuoto/`"],[13737,"The weights' version is read from the files. GPT-SoVITS models of the same version switch to these weights when they use the voice (marked **own weights** under **Which models can use it**); models of another version warn and clone as usual. **The voice keeps its clips too: the engine still needs a reference clip with the weights.** Weights exported by a training experiment are added to the voice for you."],[10606,"The Whisper encoder lives in the ASR engine and is not shared with CosyVoice's speech tokenizers"],[12236,"The windows' tokens are merged into text and timestamped segments by the pipeline's `_decode_asr`."],[8308,"The working memory set aside for a step follows the request: a language model's cache is sized by the text, not by the longest generation `max_new_tokens` allows. A generation that runs far longer than its text and outgrows the GPU runs that step again with more weights streamed, with the same result."],[10579,"Their licences (Fish Audio Research License, bilibili Model Use License) cover the code; a port is a derivative, and folding it into the GPL-3.0 `mizuoto` would conflict"],[7862,"Their results cannot be added to another engine's training datasets"],[12152,"Theme, seed colour, contrast, language, motion, last screen, Speak's last choices; kept in localStorage and synced to the server through `/api/v1/client-state/{key}`, so they follow the user across browsers"],[9324,"Then allow an engine's cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches; the output differs slightly)"],[7296,"Then binary messages: mono 16-bit little-endian PCM at the `start` rate, with `{\"type\": \"segment\", \"index\": n}` before each segment."],[13263,"Then click:"],[13909,"Then Mizuoto, in one install; add the gated engines when you want them:"],[7396,"Then open `http://<host address>:7869`; the web UI asks for the **Access token** once."],[8160,"Then restart Mizuoto. Using such a model fails with `engine_not_installed` (exit code 7) and the install command in the hint."],[10967,"then the least recently used."],[7447,"then the rest of `huggingface`, `hf-mirror`, `modelscope` in that order (with `custom` chosen, `custom` comes before these three)."],[7446,"then the source in `downloads.source`;"],[10966,"then those of models not in `engines.<id>.pinned_models` before pinned ones;"],[7409,"Then, on the host:"],[13699,"There are four kinds:"],[7206,"These routes read or write anywhere on the server's disk, so they answer only a **browser on the server machine** (a loopback client that addressed a loopback host name); anything else gets 403 `not_local`. A request forwarded through a tunnel or a reverse proxy on the same machine does not count as local."],[7477,"They are downloaded with the first model that needs them (the job's steps list them); a model whose shared files are missing is **Partly downloaded**."],[10585,"They bring version conflicts, platform limits or global state; tokenizers come from `tokenizers`, `tiktoken` and `sentencepiece`, and ONNX models' weights are converted into torch modules by an in-tree protobuf reader"],[10591,"They support only some platforms; the default path must work everywhere with unchanged results"],[10100,"Third-party modules it may import"],[13000,"This machine's devices, each GPU's memory, and the torch in use with its build, such as `torch 2.8.0 (cu128)`. When torch is missing or its build does not suit this computer, it names the right build and shows the command that installs it (`mizuoto doctor` says the same)"],[9590,"This page covers the shared conventions and common workflows; every command's options are in the Command reference, settings and environment variables in Configuration and environment variables."],[10096,"This page gives the whole picture: the packages and what each may import, the layer rules `tests/test_architecture.py` enforces, how `build_services()` assembles the services, the path of one synthesis request from the browser to an engine and back, the core's one door to model code, how engines, models, voices and remote hosts are organised, how the data folder carries over between versions, and the shared infrastructure: settings, events, jobs, errors. What happens inside the runtime is in Runtime; routes and commands are in API and CLI."],[8571,"This page groups the commands by purpose; `mizuoto --help` and each group's help list them alphabetically. Conventions and exit codes are in the Overview, settings in Configuration and environment variables."],[10407,"This page lists the conventions a change to Mizuoto must follow. Most of them are held by tests or checks: `python scripts/dev.py check` passing is the least a change needs before it is merged. The design behind each convention is in Architecture and Design references and decisions."],[14009,"This page takes the shortest path. Installation and First run have the details of each step."],[13753,"This section explains the Mizuoto web UI screen by screen. If you have not installed or started Mizuoto yet, read Quick start first. Every action in the UI has a `mizuoto` command too; see Command line."],[12177,"This section is for people who want to change Mizuoto: fix a bug, add an engine, a training method, a screen or an API route. It describes what the code **is** now, the rules it keeps and why, not how to use it (for that, see the guides and the command line)."],[12858,"This section records, engine by engine, what that took, where an engine deliberately differs, how it uses memory and runs fast, how it trains, and what the comparison found. Which engine to choose and what each offers is in Engines in depth; how an engine is written and registered is in Adding an engine."],[11530,"This site lives in `site/`. It is built on fumadocs (TanStack Start + Vite) with bun into static files (`.output/public`). `.github/workflows/site.yml` publishes it to GitHub Pages: on a push to `main` that changes `site/` (or by hand) it runs the site's checks, builds it with `VITE_BASE_PATH=/Mizuoto/` (Pages serves it under `https://licyk.github.io/Mizuoto/`; the router and the search index follow Vite's base), adds `.nojekyll`, and force-pushes the output to the `gh-pages` branch over SSH with the `GITEE_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY` secret (a key with write access to the repository). The repository's Pages settings serve that branch. `site/vercel.json` is ready for a Vercel deployment at the root path."],[10641,"Those change the recipes beyond what the presets promise"],[13038,"Three filters at the top, which combine:"],[7503,"Three scripts, run from a source checkout, make and publish a mirror: `scripts/mirror_models.py` lays out the models installed on this machine, publishes the result and checks it; `scripts/mirror_fetch.py` downloads the whole catalogue into the mirror's layout; `scripts/mirror_readme.py` writes the repository's card and licence files. Publishing is the mirror owner's step: the weights keep their own licences, and `MIRROR.json` names each file's origin."],[10133,"Three subprocess tests: `import mizuoto.core.context` loads neither torch, fastapi nor typer; `import mizuoto.cli.app` loads neither torch nor fastapi; importing the engine contract, the request context, the dummy engine, `core.inference.local` and `core.inference.runtime` loads no torch. That keeps `mizuoto version` and `mizuoto --help` fast and lets the core's tests run on the dummy engine."],[12339,"Through the stack each side computes its own voice prompt, and CAM++'s embedding is the one part not bit-exact: it differs from onnxruntime's by at most 7e-6 (cosine 0.999999999997). The flow turns that into a mel change of at most 2.7e-3, and HiFT's sine source integrates the F0 into phase (a float32 cumulative sum over the whole utterance, nine harmonics), so the error grows along the utterance: on a CosyVoice 3 English clone the SNR per half second falls from 66 to 20 dB. Upstream is just as sensitive. Its own vocoder chain fed Mizuoto's embedding gives exactly Mizuoto's audio; its own onnxruntime CAM++ with 8 threads instead of 1 gives 31 dB; random perturbations of that size give 20–33 dB. CosyVoice 2/3's language model never uses the speaker embedding, so the speech tokens are the same."],[11307,"Through the whole stack on the GPU (`perf.py --device cuda:0`), best warm run:"],[12357,"Through the whole stack, results agree closely but not bit for bit with upstream, because CAM++ is not bit-exact with onnxruntime."],[11862,"Tier"],[12915,"Tier"],[12851,"Tiers"],[11777,"Tiers and tolerances of behavioural consistency"],[10636,"Tiled decoding as an out-of-memory fallback only for some decoders (ASR, GPT-SoVITS, F5-TTS's Vocos, IndexTTS 2's BigVGAN, VoxCPM's VAE)"],[8494,"Time allowed to connect and complete the handshake"],[11848,"Time the same cases and fine-tunes phase by phase and check the audio, metrics and weights against the previous round (see Performance work)"],[8488,"Timeouts:"],[11773,"Tiny random models"],[8473,"TLS on one side only"],[1457,"TLS 设置不一致"],[10439,"To add"],[13011,"To clone a voice, models usually need the reference clip's transcript. With the speech recognition model downloaded, missing transcripts are filled in:"],[