rch，然后是 Mizuoto 及 `mizuoto[gptsovits-ja,gptsovits-ko]`（`GATED=1` 时还有 `mizuoto-indextts[ja]`）；其余依赖在构建镜像时从 PyPI 安装。"],[825,"torch、`mizuoto-fishspeech` 包"],[829,"torch、`mizuoto-indextts` 包"],[13007,"torch: the build `mizuoto doctor` names, such as `pip install \"torch>=2.8\" --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128` (the commands for each platform are in Installation)."],[5991,"torch：安装 `mizuoto doctor` 指出的构建，例如 `pip install \"torch>=2.8\" --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128`（各平台的命令见安装）。"],[11401,"torch's build is the user's (below); soxr is the resampler librosa calls; tokenizers builds the BPE transformers builds"],[8161,"torch's build must match the hardware: a CUDA build for NVIDIA (no newer than the driver supports), a ROCm build for AMD, the XPU build for Intel, PyPI's own build on Apple silicon. `mizuoto doctor` compares them and prints the command that installs the right build into Mizuoto's Python, such as:"],[8306,"torch's CUDA allocator: `native`, `async` (cudaMallocAsync), `expandable` (expandable segments); applies at the next start"],[9336,"torch's CUDA allocator: `native`, `async`, `expandable` (`auto`: native); at the next start"],[4384,"torch（≥ 2.8）、safetensors、soxr、tokenizers"],[817,"torch（2.8 或更新）"],[11430,"torchaudio, librosa, numba, resampy, scipy"],[4414,"torchaudio、librosa、numba、resampy、scipy"],[80,"train"],[7096,"train"],[13542,"Train"],[13816,"Train"],[13818,"Train"],[11946,"Trainer and StageContext"],[4930,"Trainer 与 StageContext"],[11939,"Trainers"],[10600,"Trainers reproduce upstream's recipes, including their training/inference mismatches (Qwen3-TTS's training skips `text_projection`; Fish Speech's training does not scale the codebook embeddings by 1/√11)"],[7761,"Training"],[9585,"Training"],[10865,"Training"],[12266,"Training"],[12367,"Training"],[12423,"Training"],[12472,"Training"],[12562,"Training"],[12637,"Training"],[12695,"Training"],[12769,"Training"],[12863,"Training"],[13297,"Training"],[13834,"Training"],[8395,"Training (always here)"],[13596,"Training always runs on this machine, never on a remote host; when an engine's device is on a remote host, its methods are not available. A fine-tune takes its device for itself while it runs. Choose the device under **Settings › Training › Training device**; by default it is **The engine’s device**."],[7095,"Training datasets"],[9256,"Training experiments"],[8348,"Training has its own setting, `training.attention` (**Settings** › **Training** › **Attention**). It offers only backends with a backward pass, so not SageAttention."],[11941,"Training methods in the manifest"],[13595,"Training needs nothing beyond Mizuoto and torch: every method runs in Mizuoto's own Python, each stage in a process of its own. Some methods need shared files used only for training, such as GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators (`mizuoto asset download gptsovits/s2d-v2pro`). When something is missing, the new-experiment dialog marks the method **not available** and gives the command to run."],[9503,"Training precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`"],[11652,"Training stages are the one exception: they run in their own process and seed the process-wide generators there (see Trainers)."],[11005,"Training stages run in their own process and own their device: before a GPU stage the host moves every idle model off that GPU, and the train job holds every slot of `gpu:<dev>` (`JobSpec.exclusive`). Inside the stage, `training.memory` chooses a preset of `mizuoto/training/memory.py`'s tools; a method's own hyperparameters win:"],[12009,"Training starts from a dataset. A dataset is `datasets/<slug>/`: `dataset.json`, `manifest.jsonl` (one row per clip: `id`, `audio`, `text`, `speaker`, `language`, `duration`, the rate, `excluded`, the source and `licence_tags`) and `audio/<id>.flac` (at most 48 kHz). The dataset's fingerprint is the SHA-256 of `manifest.jsonl`."],[10900,"Training tools"],[11966,"Training-only shared assets per variant (GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators); `\"*\"` for every variant"],[11177,"Training, one fine-tune per trainer (s), metrics and weight tensors identical (the stages get the CPU settings through their environment):"],[12051,"Training's memory presets (`training.memory`: `standard`, `low`, `lowest`) and tools are in `mizuoto/training/memory.py`: gradient checkpointing puts back the global generators and the trainer's own during the backward recomputation, so losses and weights do not change; `low` adds only tools that keep results, `lowest` also those that change them slightly; a method's own hyperparameters win. A stage on a GPU adds `memory/peak_mb` to its metrics, and `MethodInfo.memory_mb` estimates a run's peak per preset. Details in Memory management."],[11844,"Trains on the workspace's dataset with one implementation and keeps the experiment, metrics, previews and exports"],[8693,"Transcribe a clip with the speech recognition engine."],[9425,"Transcribe a reference clip without a transcript (needs the speech recognition model `tts.asr_model` downloaded)"],[8786,"Transcribe the clips (or this one) again with speech recognition"],[9584,"Transcribe, convert and edit"],[13429,"Transcripts and speech recognition"],[8121,"Transcripts are cached by the audio's SHA-256 and the model, so the same clip is never transcribed twice. `tts.auto_transcribe` (on by default) and `tts.asr_model` control automatic transcription; see Configuration."],[7823,"transcripts for reference clips and datasets"],[10184,"Transcripts through the `asr` engine, cached by audio SHA-256 and model"],[4062,"transformer 69.7"],[11078,"transformer 69.7"],[11424,"transformers (several incompatible versions), accelerate, huggingface_hub, peft, loralib"],[12952,"transformers' logits processors in their order; `multinomial`'s own computation without its device waits"],[4408,"transformers（多个互不兼容的版本）、accelerate、huggingface_hub、peft、loralib"],[11370,"Truncating VoxCPM's attention to exactly the filled positions: identical in bf16, not in fp32 (the kernel's blocks change); the cut at a multiple of 256 is identical in both."],[13693,"Try it"],[68,"tts"],[7084,"tts"],[13231,"Two buttons at the bottom of the page:"],[12911,"Two engines have another reference:"],[13876,"Two helper engines are built in as well: **speech recognition** (Whisper large-v3-turbo, which fills in the transcripts of reference clips) and the **dummy engine** (`dummy/default`, nothing to download; it speaks in tones so you can learn the UI first)."],[12676,"Two phases: the audio tokenizer (the voice prompt, then decoding) and the language model. The language model reruns over the whole sequence each step, so it is a `oneshot` model for weight streaming (its largest units stay on the device). Training: gradient checkpointing over the model's layers is identical, LoRA dropout included; `lowest` keeps AdamW's state in RAM (identical on the CPU)."],[12405,"Two phases: the transformer with the mel (every ODE step; guidance doubles the batch) and Vocos. If Vocos runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 frames overlapping by 32 and cross-faded (`applied.fallbacks` says so)."],[8362,"Two settings make CPU work faster without changing any result (Linux; on other systems they change nothing):"],[11723,"ty does not follow an editable install's path hook, so `pyproject.toml` sets `tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` to `packages/native/fishspeech` and `packages/native/indextts`, which resolves `mizuoto_fishspeech` and `mizuoto_indextts` from source. torch and the optional extras' packages are listed in `tool.ty.analysis.allowed-unresolved-imports`."],[11736,"ty over `mizuoto`, the gated engines, `tests` and `scripts`"],[4707,"ty 不跟随可编辑安装的路径钩子，所以 `pyproject.toml` 把 `tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` 设为 `packages/native/fishspeech` 和 `packages/native/indextts`，从源码解析 `mizuoto_fishspeech` 和 `mizuoto_indextts`。torch 和各可选附加依赖的包列在 `tool.ty.analysis.allowed-unresolved-imports` 里。"],[10800,"Type"],[14021,"T