5,"What it is"],[13756,"What it is for"],[13802,"What it is for"],[7853,"What it means"],[10836,"What it shows:"],[10486,"What Mizuoto keeps of it"],[12222,"What reproduces upstream"],[12262,"What reproduces upstream"],[12364,"What reproduces upstream"],[12420,"What reproduces upstream"],[12469,"What reproduces upstream"],[12559,"What reproduces upstream"],[12634,"What reproduces upstream"],[12691,"What reproduces upstream"],[12766,"What reproduces upstream"],[8374,"What runs where"],[11570,"What the core holds and passes: standard library only at module level"],[8642,"What the designed voice says"],[7340,"What the image contains"],[8748,"What the voice says in its reference clip (default: `Hello! This is how I sound when I read a few sentences aloud.`)"],[12996,"What to do there"],[10564,"What was not taken:"],[13090,"What you can do:"],[4366,"Wheel：`scripts/build_wheels.py`"],[4490,"wheels 阶段和镜像的基础镜像 `python:<版本>-slim`"],[11382,"Wheels: `scripts/build_wheels.py`"],[7474,"When `HF_TOKEN` is set in the environment, it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer` to huggingface.co only, never to hf-mirror, ModelScope, a custom endpoint or the mizuoto-model mirror."],[13340,"When a host is removed, the engines that ran there run on this machine again."],[13779,"When a job started on another screen finishes or fails, a message pops up at the bottom of the window; a failure's message has an **Open log** button."],[13494,"When a model is picked, its default preset is applied; the chosen voice's own default preset comes first."],[13015,"When a source lacks a file or serves it wrong, the next source is tried (the one in the settings first, then Hugging Face, hf-mirror and ModelScope)."],[13230,"When a speaker's model, voice, language, way of speaking or parameters change, every rendered line of that speaker becomes **Changed since its take**. **Level each take** under Export is a rendering setting too: changing it makes every line stale."],[8314,"When a step of a request runs out of memory anyway (an estimate was short, another program took memory), Mizuoto moves the other idle models off that GPU, leaves half of the step's own weights in RAM and runs the step again with the same random draws, so the result is the same, only slower; it tries twice. When that is not enough, and `compute.oom_fallback` is on, an engine with a cheaper way uses it (speech recognition one 30 s window at a time, GPT-SoVITS one text at a time, F5-TTS's, IndexTTS's and VoxCPM's decoders in tiles). Otherwise the request fails with `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`), and, as ComfyUI does, Mizuoto unloads every model not in use from every GPU, so the next try starts on empty devices (models on the CPU stay). If it fails again, give the engine another device, set `compute.vram_mode` to `low` or `none`, or lower `compute.max_resident_models`. Mizuoto also remembers how much memory each step really used and sets that much aside the next time."],[8291,"when a step runs out of GPU memory, run it again with more of its weights in RAM: the same result, slower"],[10638,"When a training run's estimated memory exceeds the free memory, the log warns with the preset that would fit; the run is not refused"],[13452,"When all is done the **Speak** button is back."],[8198,"When an engine fails, the request fails with `engine_error` (exit code 10), whose detail carries the exception and its traceback (**Details** under the error in the web UI; the job's `error` in `mizuoto job show <job id> --json`). The **Models in memory** panel lists an engine whose last request failed, with the error."],[13106,"When an engine has load options, its card has **Options**:"],[11682,"When an engine's device is `<host>/<device>` (for example `engines.qwen3tts.device = \"gpu-box/cuda:0\"`), `RuntimeService.engine` asks `RemoteService` for a `RemoteEngine`: a session with the `mizuoto agent` on that host for one engine on one device. The agent is a whole Mizuoto with its own data folder, models and runtime; it runs the engine in its own process exactly as a host does. `RemoteEngineHandle` answers the same calls as `LocalHandle`. For the user-facing set-up, see Remote engines."],[8186,"When every source fails the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12), whose detail lists the sources tried and the last errors."],[10964,"When free memory falls short, idle components on the same device give up the shortfall, in this order:"],[7295,"When generation starts: `{\"type\": \"start\", \"job_id\": …, \"sample_rate\": 24000, \"granularity\": \"token\" | \"segment\" | \"emulated\"}`."],[8170,"When memory runs out during a request anyway, Mizuoto runs the step again with more of its weights in RAM and the same random draws (the same result, slower); with `compute.oom_fallback` it then tries a cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches). `compute.gpu_jobs` (default 1) sets how many jobs run at once on one GPU; a job waiting for the GPU can be started beside the running one with **Run anyway** when the memory suffices. `compute.inference_jobs` (default 1) sets how many synthesis jobs run at once across all engines and devices. More in Performance."],[8383,"When one machine has the GPU and another is where you use Mizuoto, an engine can run on the GPU machine. That machine runs `mizuoto agent` (the **agent** below); the machine you use (the **host** below) adds it as a remote host and sets the engine's device to `<name>/<device>`, for example `gpu-box/cuda:0`. Synthesis, streaming and cancelling then work as they do locally; only the engine, and the models it loads, run on the agent."],[9451,"When requests are batched: Performance."],[8380,"When something fails"],[8133,"When something goes wrong, read the job's log first (**Log** in the **Jobs** panel, or `mizuoto job log <job id>`), then run `mizuoto doctor`: it checks torch's build against the hardware, whether each engine is available and which optional extras are missing, and gives the commands that fix what 