when the weights move or the model unloads. The real 0.5B and 1.5 give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.6–1.9 times faster per request."],[12453,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the model wholly on its device) `generate.Decoder` keeps fixed tensors per loaded model: the slow step runs as one graph per stretch between attention calls (`LayerSteps`), and the frame's draws, repetition-aware sampling and the fast transformer as one graph. The sampling settings are device tensors filled per request, so one set of graphs serves every request. The codes are identical, 2.2–2.5 times faster per frame on the decode loop."],[8312,"With `compute.vram_mode = high` (**Whole or not at all**), Mizuoto always tries to load a model whole, whatever the catalogue's estimate and the card's free memory say, as ComfyUI does. It first moves idle models off that GPU to make room, then copies the weights. The request fails only when an allocation really fails: the code is `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`; exit code 9 on the command line), and every model not in use is then unloaded from every GPU (see below). With `compute.gpu_jobs` above 1, a request short of room while another request holds the GPU first waits for it to finish (up to 10 minutes), then tries."],[7445,"With `downloads.repository` set to `mizuoto-model` (the default), the mizuoto-model mirror first;"],[7451,"With `downloads.verify_checksums` (**Verify checksums**, on by default) off, only sizes are checked."],[8152,"With `server.access_token` set, the UI shows the **Access token** dialog (\"This server asks for its access token.\"); enter it once. An API request without it gets 401 `auth_required`; send it as an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, the `mizuoto_token` cookie or a `?token=` query parameter (see HTTP API)."],[10298,"With `tts.micro_batch` on, `TtsService._batch_group()` gives a speak job a `JobSpec.group` when the variant has the `batch` capability with `max_batch > 1`, 